{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789366409652,"sessionID":"ses_f6176138cffeODZD3dhSK78dPo","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-be0bf6507e8ba342","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening/research"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening/research</path>\n<type>directory</type>\n<entries>\nalternatives/\nangles.txt\ndeep-research-findings-registry.json\nfanout-attribution.md\nfindings-registry.json\niterations/\nlineages/\nobservability-events.jsonl\nopen-questions/\norchestration-summary.json\nsynthesis.md\nworktree-symlinks/\n\n(12 entries)\n</entries>","metadata":{"preview":"alternatives/\nangles.txt\ndeep-research-findings-registry.json\nfanout-attribution.md\nfindings-registry.json\niterations/\nlineages/\nobservability-events.jsonl\nopen-questions/\norchestration-summary.json\nsynthesis.md\nworktree-symlinks/","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"directory","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening/research","entries":["alternatives/","angles.txt","deep-research-findings-registry.json","fanout-attribution.md","findings-registry.json","iterations/","lineages/","observability-events.jsonl","open-questions/","orchestration-summary.json","synthesis.md","worktree-symlinks/"],"offset":1,"totalEntries":12,"truncated":false}},"title":"specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening/research","time":{"start":1789366409644,"end":1789366409651}},"id":"prt_09e8c96fc001oU4ev6hg0uMyIM","sessionID":"ses_f6176138cffeODZD3dhSK78dPo","messageID":"msg_09e8c63ff001OliqAtpEk6lZp7"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789366410229,"sessionID":"ses_f6176138cffeODZD3dhSK78dPo","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-b5f9b998869e7b86","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/.opencode/commands/deep/research.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/.opencode/commands/deep/research.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: ---\n2: description: \"Autonomous deep-research loop: iterative investigation with convergence detection. Modes :auto, :confirm.\"\n3: argument-hint: \"<topic> [:auto|:confirm] [--spec-folder=PATH] [--max-iterations=N] [--executor=TYPE] [--concurrency=N] [--dry-run]\"\n4: allowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob, Task, WebFetch\n5: ---\n6: \n7: # Deep Start Research Loop\n8: \n9: Thin router for the deep-research loop. This command verifies the runtime agent, resolves setup and execution mode, loads the presentation contract, then executes the owned workflow YAML.\n10: \n11: ## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n12: \n13: Do not dispatch agents from this Markdown file. Agent dispatch, workflow steps, artifact-writing behavior, convergence detection, synthesis, and memory save behavior are owned by the workflow YAML assets.\n14: \n15: Load the presentation contract before showing startup questions, dashboards, checkpoint text, success output, failure output, examples, or next-step prompts.\n16: \n17: \n18: > **EXECUTION PROTOCOL -- READ FIRST**\n19: >\n20: > This command runs a structured YAML workflow. Do NOT dispatch agents from this document.\n21: >\n22: > **YOUR FIRST ACTION (HARD-BLOCK gate — do not skip):**\n23: > 1. Run the Unified Setup Phase (BLOCKED gate) through the presentation contract and resolve:\n24: >    - `research_topic`\n25: >    - `spec_folder`\n26: >    - `execution_mode`\n27: >    - `maxIterations`\n28: >    - `convergenceThreshold`\n29: >    - `stop_policy` (default `convergence` unless `--stop-policy=max-iterations` is present)\n30: >    - `dry_run` (default false unless `--dry-run` is present)\n31: > 2. Load the corresponding YAML file from `assets/` only after all setup values are resolved:\n32: >    - Auto: `deep-research-auto.yaml`\n33: >    - Confirm: `deep-research-confirm.yaml`\n34: > 3. Execute the YAML workflow step by step using those resolved values\n35: >\n36: > This command is **general-agent based** — it orchestrates the deep-research loop. The Unified Setup Phase (the BLOCKED gate) is a HARD BLOCK; it may not be skipped.\n37: \n38: ### MANDATORY INPUT GATE\n39: \n40: - **DO NOT** dispatch any agent from this document.\n41: - **ALL** agent dispatching is handled by the YAML workflow steps.\n42: - **MARKDOWN OWNS SETUP**: resolve setup inputs here first, then hand off to YAML.\n43: - **YAML START CONDITION**: do not load YAML until ALL required inputs are bound:\n44:   - `research_topic`, `spec_folder`, `execution_mode`, `maxIterations`, `convergenceThreshold`, `stop_policy`\n45:   - `dry_run` is normalized to `true` or `false`; absence means `false`\n46: \n47: For `:confirm` or no suffix, the consolidated setup prompt in the presentation contract MUST be the first visible response. For `:auto`, do not emit the consolidated setup prompt by default; use the auto setup resolution rules in the presentation contract and fail fast when required fields cannot be resolved.\n48: \n49: > **Canonical mode syntax:** use attached command suffixes (`/deep:research:auto`, `/deep:research:confirm`).\n50: \n51: > **Note:** Late-INIT `spec.md` detection and bounded `spec.md` mutations follow\n52: > `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md`.\n53: > Acquire `{spec_folder}/research/.deep-research.lock` before `folder_state` classification and keep `research/research.md` as the source of truth for any generated findings sync.\n54: > Targeted strict validation after deep-research spec mutations uses the Node validation orchestrator.\n55: \n56: ### AUTONOMOUS EXECUTION DIRECTIVE (:auto)\n57: \n58: > Read this first. It is an imperative to you, the executor — not background information.\n59: \n60: You were invoked via `opencode run --command deep/research` with the `:auto` suffix and a bound spec_folder and target in your message. The `:auto` suffix plus the bound spec_folder mean setup is ALREADY resolved. Therefore:\n61: \n62: - DO NOT emit the consolidated setup question (target/mode, research topic, Spec Folder A/B/C/D/E, execution mode, max iterations, executor). The bound spec_folder is your write authority; do not ask which spec folder should own the writes.\n63: - DO NOT halt for the repo-wide `CLAUDE.md` Gate-3 documentation gate. Under AUTONOMOUS execution with a validated prebound spec folder, Gate 3 is already satisfied by that folder (the prebound spec folder is your write authority).\n64: - PROCEED immediately: load the auto workflow YAML and dispatch the `deep-research` agent to run ONE iteration of the research loop over the bound target.\n65: - DISPATCH ONLY: you dispatch `deep-research` to run one iteration; you do NOT read, edit, patch, or run the research loop over the target yourself. The auto workflow YAML owns the loop itself — setup, dispatch-per-iteration, reducer sync, convergence checks, synthesis, and all loop-level artifact writes; the `deep-research` leaf owns only its own single-iteration artifacts — mixing your own inline work with the dispatch is a route violation.\n66: - ROUTE PROOF: dispatch through the auto workflow with its prompt pack so `deep-research` writes each iteration state record with the route-proof fields present — `target_agent: \"deep-research\"`, `resolved_route`, `agent_definition_loaded: true`, and `mode: \"research\"`. A completed run whose iteration state records omit these fields is an incomplete delegation and does not pass.\n67: \n68: Your job is to DISPATCH `deep-research` to run ONE iteration of the research loop over the bound target — NOT to run the loop yourself, and NOT to review, analyze, or summarize this contract. The auto workflow YAML owns the loop itself (setup, dispatch-per-iteration, reducer sync, convergence, synthesis, and loop-level writes). This contract is your instruction set; the research target is the bound spec_folder/target named in your message, never this document.\n69: \n70: ---\n71: \n72: ## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n73: \n74: | Purpose | Asset |\n75: |---------|-------|\n76: | Presentation source of truth | `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt` |\n77: | Auto workflow | `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml` |\n78: | Confirm workflow | `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-confirm.yaml` |\n79: \n80: ---\n81: \n82: ## 3. MODE ROUTING\n83: \n84: 1. Parse `$ARGUMENTS` for attached suffixes: `:auto` sets `execution_mode = AUTONOMOUS`; `:confirm` sets `execution_mode = INTERACTIVE`; no suffix sets `execution_mode = ASK`.\n85: 2. Treat `--max-iterations`, `--convergence`, `--lineage-timeout-hours`, `--stop-policy`, `--dry-run`, `--spec-folder`, `--executor`, `--model`, `--config-dir`, `--reasoning-effort`, `--service-tier`, `--executor-timeout`, `--iters`, `--label`, `--count`, `--executors`, `--concurrency`, and `--no-resource-map` as workflow inputs, not execution modes.\n86: 3. For `:auto`, resolve setup from `$ARGUMENTS` flags, any `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` marker block, scope-extracted spec-folder paths, and the presentation contract's default resolution table. When all required fields are resolved, persist `{artifact_dir}/deep-research-config.json`, bind runtime YAML placeholders, and load `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml`.\n87: 4. In `:auto`, ask a targeted Tier-2 question only for `spec_folder` when the topic is present, names no resolvable spec folder, and the folder choice is ambiguous. Missing `research_topic` is absence, not ambiguity; use the named-missing-inputs fail-fast format from the auto-mode contract and do not load YAML.\n88: 5. For `:confirm`, use the presentation contract's consolidated setup prompt to bind missing setup values, then load `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-confirm.yaml`.\n89: 6. For no suffix, use the presentation contract's consolidated setup prompt to choose execution mode and bind missing setup values, then route the resolved interactive choice to the matching YAML.\n90: 7. Lightweight read-only discovery for related spec folders or prior memory may support setup, but it must feed the single consolidated prompt and never split setup questions.\n91: 8. After the selected workflow asset is loaded, execute it step by step using the resolved setup values.\n92: \n93: ### Workflow Flag Surface\n94: \n95: The argument hint names the invocation shape; the whole flag surface is here. Every flag below\n96: is a workflow input, never an execution mode, and the presentation asset owns how each one binds\n97: into `config`.\n98: \n99: | Flag | Value | Effect |\n100: |------|-------|--------|\n101: | `--spec-folder` | `PATH` | Binds the packet that owns this run's writes. |\n102: | `--max-iterations` | `N` | Hard ceiling on loop iterations. |\n103: | `--convergence` | `N` | Threshold the loop must clear before convergence may stop it. |\n104: | `--convergence-mode` | `default` \\| `off` \\| `sliding-window` \\| `divergent` | `default` keeps the anti-convergence `minIterations` floor. `off` disables convergence-driven STOP while max-iterations, pause and halt stay active. `sliding-window` scores novelty over a bounded window, five snapshots by default, on the ordinary legal-stop path. `divergent` sends a `composite_converged` or `all_questions_answered` stop into a one-round three-seat Council pivot instead of ending the run, at proportionally higher cost. |\n105: | `--lineage-timeout-hours` | `N` | See Lineage Timeout Flag below. |\n106: | `--stop-policy` | `convergence` \\| `max-iterations` | See Stop Policy Flag below. |\n107: | `--no-resource-map` | no value | Suppresses the `research/resource-map.md` write; `research.md` still emits. |\n108: | `--dry-run` | no value | See Dry-Run Flag below. |\n109: | `--executor` | `TYPE` | Selects the executor kind, and is repeatable. Each occurrence opens a group accepting `--model=X`, `--config-dir=PATH`, `--reasoning-effort=LEVEL`, `--service-tier=TIER`, `--executor-timeout=SECONDS`, `--iters=N`, `--count=N` and `--label=X`. Which of those a given kind supports, and the fail-fast on an unsupported pairing, are in the presentation asset. |\n110: | `--executors` | `JSON` | Escape hatch declaring the whole fan-out matrix in one value instead of repeated `--executor` groups. |\n111: | `--concurrency` | `N` | Caps concurrent lineages in the fan-out pool. Default `2`. |\n112: \n113: Fan-out policy: zero or one `--executor` and no `--executors` runs the single-executor path;\n114: two or more `--executor` flags, an `--executors` value, or any `--count` above 1 switches to\n115: fan-out, one independent lineage per label. Under `:auto` a `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` block in\n116: the prompt body binds the same values without an interactive prompt.\n117: \n118: ### Lineage Timeout Flag\n119: \n120: `--lineage-timeout-hours <N>` optionally narrows the per-lineage wall-clock timeout ceiling below the default 4 hours; values above the hard 4-hour maximum are rejected, and omitting the flag keeps the 4h default.\n121: \n122: ### Stop Policy Flag\n123: \n124: `--stop-policy <convergence|max-iterations>` selects whether convergence may stop the loop early. The default `convergence` stops at legal convergence or `config.maxIterations`, whichever comes first; `max-iterations` treats convergence as telemetry only and forces the loop to continue until `config.maxIterations`, which is useful for forced-depth runs.\n125: \n126: ### Dry-Run Flag\n127: \n128: `--dry-run` is a first-class flag on the confirm flow, not a third execution mode. It still performs real setup resolution, artifact-root resolution, focus selection, prompt rendering, and convergence reads when those steps can run without side effects.\n129: \n130: When `dry_run=true`, the confirm YAML emits `dry_run_halt` JSONL preview lines to terminal output instead of appending to the live state log, and halts before executor dispatch, persistent state mutation, reducer refresh, or child-lineage spawn. A fresh packet will stop at the first persistent state boundary; an existing packet can read current state and convergence signals, render the next prompt for preview, then stop before dispatch.\n131: \n132: ---\n133: \n134: ## 4. EXECUTION TARGETS\n135: \n136: | Mode | Target |\n137: |------|----------|\n138: | `:auto` | `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml` |\n139: | `:confirm` or interactive choice | `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-confirm.yaml` |\n140: \n141: ---\n142: \n143: ## 5. PRESENTATION BOUNDARY\n144: \n145: The following content lives only in `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt`:\n146: \n147: - Startup-question wording, consolidated setup prompt text, and reply format examples.\n148: - `:auto` pre-bound setup answer schema, default resolution table, targeted-ask rules, and fail-fast display references.\n149: - Dashboard/checkpoint layout, workflow overview display, convergence-threshold explanation, and user-facing examples.\n150: - Success and failure result templates, error-handling display, and memory-integration result wording.\n151: - Next-step suggestions, command-chain wording, skill-reference text, and offline optimization notes.\n152: \n153: ---\n154: \n155: ## 6. WORKFLOW SUMMARY\n156: \n157: The selected YAML workflow initializes deep-research state, dispatches fresh `@deep-research` LEAF agents per iteration, evaluates convergence, synthesizes `{artifact_dir}/research.md`, optionally emits `{artifact_dir}/resource-map.md`, and refreshes continuity through canonical spec docs. This command does not proceed to implementation.\n158: \n159: For code review and quality auditing, route to `/deep:review`. Research path: `/deep:research` → `/speckit:plan` → `/speckit:implement`; review path: `/deep:review` → (if issues) `/speckit:plan` → `/speckit:implement`.\n\n(End of file - total 159 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"---\ndescription: \"Autonomous deep-research loop: iterative investigation with convergence detection. Modes :auto, :confirm.\"\nargument-hint: \"<topic> [:auto|:confirm] [--spec-folder=PATH] [--max-iterations=N] [--executor=TYPE] [--concurrency=N] [--dry-run]\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob, Task, WebFetch\n---\n\n# Deep Start Research Loop\n\nThin router for the deep-research loop. This command verifies the runtime agent, resolves setup and execution mode, loads the presentation contract, then executes the owned workflow YAML.\n\n## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n\nDo not dispatch agents from this Markdown file. Agent dispatch, workflow steps, artifact-writing behavior, convergence detection, synthesis, and memory save behavior are owned by the workflow YAML assets.\n\nLoad the presentation contract before showing startup questions, dashboards, checkpoint text, success output, failure output, examples, or next-step prompts.\n\n\n> **EXECUTION PROTOCOL -- READ FIRST**\n>\n> This command runs a structured YAML workflow. Do NOT dispatch agents from this document.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/.opencode/commands/deep/research.md","text":"---\ndescription: \"Autonomous deep-research loop: iterative investigation with convergence detection. Modes :auto, :confirm.\"\nargument-hint: \"<topic> [:auto|:confirm] [--spec-folder=PATH] [--max-iterations=N] [--executor=TYPE] [--concurrency=N] [--dry-run]\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob, Task, WebFetch\n---\n\n# Deep Start Research Loop\n\nThin router for the deep-research loop. This command verifies the runtime agent, resolves setup and execution mode, loads the presentation contract, then executes the owned workflow YAML.\n\n## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n\nDo not dispatch agents from this Markdown file. Agent dispatch, workflow steps, artifact-writing behavior, convergence detection, synthesis, and memory save behavior are owned by the workflow YAML assets.\n\nLoad the presentation contract before showing startup questions, dashboards, checkpoint text, success output, failure output, examples, or next-step prompts.\n\n\n> **EXECUTION PROTOCOL -- READ FIRST**\n>\n> This command runs a structured YAML workflow. Do NOT dispatch agents from this document.\n>\n> **YOUR FIRST ACTION (HARD-BLOCK gate — do not skip):**\n> 1. Run the Unified Setup Phase (BLOCKED gate) through the presentation contract and resolve:\n>    - `research_topic`\n>    - `spec_folder`\n>    - `execution_mode`\n>    - `maxIterations`\n>    - `convergenceThreshold`\n>    - `stop_policy` (default `convergence` unless `--stop-policy=max-iterations` is present)\n>    - `dry_run` (default false unless `--dry-run` is present)\n> 2. Load the corresponding YAML file from `assets/` only after all setup values are resolved:\n>    - Auto: `deep-research-auto.yaml`\n>    - Confirm: `deep-research-confirm.yaml`\n> 3. Execute the YAML workflow step by step using those resolved values\n>\n> This command is **general-agent based** — it orchestrates the deep-research loop. The Unified Setup Phase (the BLOCKED gate) is a HARD BLOCK; it may not be skipped.\n\n### MANDATORY INPUT GATE\n\n- **DO NOT** dispatch any agent from this document.\n- **ALL** agent dispatching is handled by the YAML workflow steps.\n- **MARKDOWN OWNS SETUP**: resolve setup inputs here first, then hand off to YAML.\n- **YAML START CONDITION**: do not load YAML until ALL required inputs are bound:\n  - `research_topic`, `spec_folder`, `execution_mode`, `maxIterations`, `convergenceThreshold`, `stop_policy`\n  - `dry_run` is normalized to `true` or `false`; absence means `false`\n\nFor `:confirm` or no suffix, the consolidated setup prompt in the presentation contract MUST be the first visible response. For `:auto`, do not emit the consolidated setup prompt by default; use the auto setup resolution rules in the presentation contract and fail fast when required fields cannot be resolved.\n\n> **Canonical mode syntax:** use attached command suffixes (`/deep:research:auto`, `/deep:research:confirm`).\n\n> **Note:** Late-INIT `spec.md` detection and bounded `spec.md` mutations follow\n> `.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md`.\n> Acquire `{spec_folder}/research/.deep-research.lock` before `folder_state` classification and keep `research/research.md` as the source of truth for any generated findings sync.\n> Targeted strict validation after deep-research spec mutations uses the Node validation orchestrator.\n\n### AUTONOMOUS EXECUTION DIRECTIVE (:auto)\n\n> Read this first. It is an imperative to you, the executor — not background information.\n\nYou were invoked via `opencode run --command deep/research` with the `:auto` suffix and a bound spec_folder and target in your message. The `:auto` suffix plus the bound spec_folder mean setup is ALREADY resolved. Therefore:\n\n- DO NOT emit the consolidated setup question (target/mode, research topic, Spec Folder A/B/C/D/E, execution mode, max iterations, executor). The bound spec_folder is your write authority; do not ask which spec folder should own the writes.\n- DO NOT halt for the repo-wide `CLAUDE.md` Gate-3 documentation gate. Under AUTONOMOUS execution with a validated prebound spec folder, Gate 3 is already satisfied by that folder (the prebound spec folder is your write authority).\n- PROCEED immediately: load the auto workflow YAML and dispatch the `deep-research` agent to run ONE iteration of the research loop over the bound target.\n- DISPATCH ONLY: you dispatch `deep-research` to run one iteration; you do NOT read, edit, patch, or run the research loop over the target yourself. The auto workflow YAML owns the loop itself — setup, dispatch-per-iteration, reducer sync, convergence checks, synthesis, and all loop-level artifact writes; the `deep-research` leaf owns only its own single-iteration artifacts — mixing your own inline work with the dispatch is a route violation.\n- ROUTE PROOF: dispatch through the auto workflow with its prompt pack so `deep-research` writes each iteration state record with the route-proof fields present — `target_agent: \"deep-research\"`, `resolved_route`, `agent_definition_loaded: true`, and `mode: \"research\"`. A completed run whose iteration state records omit these fields is an incomplete delegation and does not pass.\n\nYour job is to DISPATCH `deep-research` to run ONE iteration of the research loop over the bound target — NOT to run the loop yourself, and NOT to review, analyze, or summarize this contract. The auto workflow YAML owns the loop itself (setup, dispatch-per-iteration, reducer sync, convergence, synthesis, and loop-level writes). This contract is your instruction set; the research target is the bound spec_folder/target named in your message, never this document.\n\n---\n\n## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n\n| Purpose | Asset |\n|---------|-------|\n| Presentation source of truth | `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt` |\n| Auto workflow | `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml` |\n| Confirm workflow | `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-confirm.yaml` |\n\n---\n\n## 3. MODE ROUTING\n\n1. Parse `$ARGUMENTS` for attached suffixes: `:auto` sets `execution_mode = AUTONOMOUS`; `:confirm` sets `execution_mode = INTERACTIVE`; no suffix sets `execution_mode = ASK`.\n2. Treat `--max-iterations`, `--convergence`, `--lineage-timeout-hours`, `--stop-policy`, `--dry-run`, `--spec-folder`, `--executor`, `--model`, `--config-dir`, `--reasoning-effort`, `--service-tier`, `--executor-timeout`, `--iters`, `--label`, `--count`, `--executors`, `--concurrency`, and `--no-resource-map` as workflow inputs, not execution modes.\n3. For `:auto`, resolve setup from `$ARGUMENTS` flags, any `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` marker block, scope-extracted spec-folder paths, and the presentation contract's default resolution table. When all required fields are resolved, persist `{artifact_dir}/deep-research-config.json`, bind runtime YAML placeholders, and load `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml`.\n4. In `:auto`, ask a targeted Tier-2 question only for `spec_folder` when the topic is present, names no resolvable spec folder, and the folder choice is ambiguous. Missing `research_topic` is absence, not ambiguity; use the named-missing-inputs fail-fast format from the auto-mode contract and do not load YAML.\n5. For `:confirm`, use the presentation contract's consolidated setup prompt to bind missing setup values, then load `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-confirm.yaml`.\n6. For no suffix, use the presentation contract's consolidated setup prompt to choose execution mode and bind missing setup values, then route the resolved interactive choice to the matching YAML.\n7. Lightweight read-only discovery for related spec folders or prior memory may support setup, but it must feed the single consolidated prompt and never split setup questions.\n8. After the selected workflow asset is loaded, execute it step by step using the resolved setup values.\n\n### Workflow Flag Surface\n\nThe argument hint names the invocation shape; the whole flag surface is here. Every flag below\nis a workflow input, never an execution mode, and the presentation asset owns how each one binds\ninto `config`.\n\n| Flag | Value | Effect |\n|------|-------|--------|\n| `--spec-folder` | `PATH` | Binds the packet that owns this run's writes. |\n| `--max-iterations` | `N` | Hard ceiling on loop iterations. |\n| `--convergence` | `N` | Threshold the loop must clear before convergence may stop it. |\n| `--convergence-mode` | `default` \\| `off` \\| `sliding-window` \\| `divergent` | `default` keeps the anti-convergence `minIterations` floor. `off` disables convergence-driven STOP while max-iterations, pause and halt stay active. `sliding-window` scores novelty over a bounded window, five snapshots by default, on the ordinary legal-stop path. `divergent` sends a `composite_converged` or `all_questions_answered` stop into a one-round three-seat Council pivot instead of ending the run, at proportionally higher cost. |\n| `--lineage-timeout-hours` | `N` | See Lineage Timeout Flag below. |\n| `--stop-policy` | `convergence` \\| `max-iterations` | See Stop Policy Flag below. |\n| `--no-resource-map` | no value | Suppresses the `research/resource-map.md` write; `research.md` still emits. |\n| `--dry-run` | no value | See Dry-Run Flag below. |\n| `--executor` | `TYPE` | Selects the executor kind, and is repeatable. Each occurrence opens a group accepting `--model=X`, `--config-dir=PATH`, `--reasoning-effort=LEVEL`, `--service-tier=TIER`, `--executor-timeout=SECONDS`, `--iters=N`, `--count=N` and `--label=X`. Which of those a given kind supports, and the fail-fast on an unsupported pairing, are in the presentation asset. |\n| `--executors` | `JSON` | Escape hatch declaring the whole fan-out matrix in one value instead of repeated `--executor` groups. |\n| `--concurrency` | `N` | Caps concurrent lineages in the fan-out pool. Default `2`. |\n\nFan-out policy: zero or one `--executor` and no `--executors` runs the single-executor path;\ntwo or more `--executor` flags, an `--executors` value, or any `--count` above 1 switches to\nfan-out, one independent lineage per label. Under `:auto` a `PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS:` block in\nthe prompt body binds the same values without an interactive prompt.\n\n### Lineage Timeout Flag\n\n`--lineage-timeout-hours <N>` optionally narrows the per-lineage wall-clock timeout ceiling below the default 4 hours; values above the hard 4-hour maximum are rejected, and omitting the flag keeps the 4h default.\n\n### Stop Policy Flag\n\n`--stop-policy <convergence|max-iterations>` selects whether convergence may stop the loop early. The default `convergence` stops at legal convergence or `config.maxIterations`, whichever comes first; `max-iterations` treats convergence as telemetry only and forces the loop to continue until `config.maxIterations`, which is useful for forced-depth runs.\n\n### Dry-Run Flag\n\n`--dry-run` is a first-class flag on the confirm flow, not a third execution mode. It still performs real setup resolution, artifact-root resolution, focus selection, prompt rendering, and convergence reads when those steps can run without side effects.\n\nWhen `dry_run=true`, the confirm YAML emits `dry_run_halt` JSONL preview lines to terminal output instead of appending to the live state log, and halts before executor dispatch, persistent state mutation, reducer refresh, or child-lineage spawn. A fresh packet will stop at the first persistent state boundary; an existing packet can read current state and convergence signals, render the next prompt for preview, then stop before dispatch.\n\n---\n\n## 4. EXECUTION TARGETS\n\n| Mode | Target |\n|------|----------|\n| `:auto` | `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml` |\n| `:confirm` or interactive choice | `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-confirm.yaml` |\n\n---\n\n## 5. PRESENTATION BOUNDARY\n\nThe following content lives only in `.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-presentation.txt`:\n\n- Startup-question wording, consolidated setup prompt text, and reply format examples.\n- `:auto` pre-bound setup answer schema, default resolution table, targeted-ask rules, and fail-fast display references.\n- Dashboard/checkpoint layout, workflow overview display, convergence-threshold explanation, and user-facing examples.\n- Success and failure result templates, error-handling display, and memory-integration result wording.\n- Next-step suggestions, command-chain wording, skill-reference text, and offline optimization notes.\n\n---\n\n## 6. WORKFLOW SUMMARY\n\nThe selected YAML workflow initializes deep-research state, dispatches fresh `@deep-research` LEAF agents per iteration, evaluates convergence, synthesizes `{artifact_dir}/research.md`, optionally emits `{artifact_dir}/resource-map.md`, and refreshes continuity through canonical spec docs. This command does not proceed to implementation.\n\nFor code review and quality auditing, route to `/deep:review`. Research path: `/deep:research` → `/speckit:plan` → `/speckit:implement`; review path: `/deep:review` → (if issues) `/speckit:plan` → `/speckit:implement`.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":159,"totalLines":159,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/commands/deep/research.md","time":{"start":1789366410198,"end":1789366410227}},"id":"prt_09e8c99ad001GEqo1zY7Ygl9mz","sessionID":"ses_f6176138cffeODZD3dhSK78dPo","messageID":"msg_09e8c63ff001OliqAtpEk6lZp7"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1789366411269,"sessionID":"ses_f6176138cffeODZD3dhSK78dPo","part":{"id":"prt_09e8c9fff001bybehg9t17G15n","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"22eb2f58f5c1c36e3a53c08312f1857a6833f85f","messageID":"msg_09e8c63ff001OliqAtpEk6lZp7","sessionID":"ses_f6176138cffeODZD3dhSK78dPo","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":35400,"input":12515,"output":71,"reasoning":414,"cache":{"write":0,"read":22400}},"cost":0.00178257}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1789366419026,"sessionID":"ses_f6176138cffeODZD3dhSK78dPo","part":{"id":"prt_09e8cbe510012tQnX788IHrVKT","messageID":"msg_09e8ca452001644sJS5GpNu9E8","sessionID":"ses_f6176138cffeODZD3dhSK78dPo","snapshot":"1cc0e6131ba475722e0249515f7e7108a8c00ee4","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789366420524,"sessionID":"ses_f6176138cffeODZD3dhSK78dPo","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-bbb7477c75a4b05f","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n2: # DEEP RESEARCH: AUTONOMOUS DEEP RESEARCH LOOP (AUTO MODE)\n3: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n4: # YAML PREDICATE GRAMMAR CONTRACT (S7 / M11):\n5: # - This asset does not currently use typed BooleanExpr predicates under\n6: #   `when:`; flow control is branch-label-driven (`on_resume`, `on_fresh`,\n7: #   `on_restart`, etc.). Retain the existing shape.\n8: # - `after:` carries prose timing / narrative notes if needed; `when:` in\n9: #   this file is reserved for future typed predicates and must NOT carry\n10: #   free-form narrative prose.\n11: # - See `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/predicates/boolean-expr.ts`\n12: #   for the canonical BooleanExpr grammar.\n13: #\n14: # GATE 3 CLASSIFICATION (T-YML-DPR-01 / paired with T-DOC-03 R50-001):\n15: # - `resume` is a tested WRITE-PATH that produces `iteration-NNN.md` files\n16: #   and JSONL state-log appends. The workflow classifies resume as\n17: #   write-path below (see `gate3_classification` fields) so Gate 3 trigger\n18: #   extraction can surface resume correctly rather than false-negative.\n19: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n20: role: Deep Research Loop Manager\n21: purpose: Iterative deep research with convergence detection\n22: action: Run deep-research loop from initialization through synthesis\n23: operating_mode:\n24:   workflow: iterative_loop\n25:   workflow_compliance: MANDATORY\n26:   workflow_execution: autonomous\n27:   approvals: none\n28:   tracking: progressive_research_state\n29:   validation: convergence_detection\n30: \n31: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n32: # OPERATING PRINCIPLES\n33: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n34: operating_principles:\n35:   core: \"Fresh context per iteration + externalized state = no context degradation\"\n36:   approach: \"Dispatch focused agent, evaluate convergence, repeat or stop\"\n37:   mandate: \"Never hold findings in memory; write everything to files\"\n38: \n39: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n40: # USER INPUTS (from setup phase)\n41: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n42: user_inputs:\n43:   research_topic: \"[RESEARCH_TOPIC] - Topic to investigate deeply. REQUIRED.\"\n44:   spec_folder: \"[SPEC_FOLDER] - Spec folder path. REQUIRED.\"\n45:   max_iterations: \"[MAX_ITERATIONS] - Maximum loop iterations. Default: 10.\"\n46:   convergence_threshold: \"[CONVERGENCE_THRESHOLD] - Stop threshold. Default: 0.05.\"\n47:   convergence_mode: \"[default|off|sliding-window|divergent] - Convergence policy modifier. Default: default.\"\n48:   stop_policy: \"[convergence|max-iterations] - Convergence stop policy; max-iterations forces the loop to run every iteration. Default: convergence.\"\n49: \n50: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n51: # CONTEXT LOADING\n52: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n53: context_loading:\n54:   trigger: \"At workflow START, before phase_init\"\n55:   purpose: \"Load prior research context for the topic and buffer it until strategy.md exists\"\n56:   retrieval:\n57:     mechanism: \"continuity-ladder-then-ripgrep\"\n58:     note: \"File reads only. Nothing here needs a running daemon, and every step is reproducible by hand.\"\n59:     ladder:\n60:       - \"{spec_folder}/handover.md when present\"\n61:       - \"the _memory.continuity frontmatter block in {spec_folder}/implementation-summary.md\"\n62:       - \"the packet's canonical spec docs, spec.md and decision-record.md, for what the first two steps leave open\"\n63:     free_text_recipe: \"rg --no-config --json --fixed-strings --ignore-case -C 2 --glob '*.md' --glob '!**/z_archive/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**' -- '{research_topic}' specs .opencode\"\n64:     recipe_contract: \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md\"\n65:     exit_status: \"0 is a hit set, 1 is a clean no-hit, 2 or higher is a failure that must be surfaced instead of reported as no-hit\"\n66:     ranking: \"Ripgrep does not rank. Order the hits caller-side with the tuple in retrieval-conventions.md section 5.\"\n67:   when_to_skip: [\"User says 'skip context' or 'fresh start'\"]\n68:   behavior:\n69:     if_context_found: \"Store full results as prior_context plus a concise prior_context_summary; inject after strategy.md is created.\"\n70:     if_no_context: \"Set prior_context and prior_context_summary to 'None' and continue.\"\n71: \n72: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n73: # SKILL REFERENCE\n74: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n75: skill_reference:\n76:   skill: system-deep-loop\n77:   skill_md: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md\n78:   references:\n79:     loop_protocol: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md\n80:     spec_check_protocol: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md\n81:     state_format: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/state/state-format.md\n82:     convergence: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence.md\n83:   templates:\n84:     config: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-config.json\n85:     strategy: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md\n86: \n87: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n88: # AGENT CONFIGURATION\n89: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n90: agent_config:\n91:   agent: deep-research\n92:   agent_file: \".opencode/agents/deep-research.md\"\n93:   # Canonical path. Runtime-specific directories (e.g. .claude/agents/) reference this source.\n94:   model: opus\n95:   leaf_only: true\n96:   tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob, WebFetch]\n97:   mcp_servers: []\n98:   tool_call_budget: { target: 8, max: 12 }\n99: \n100: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n101: # STATE FILE PATHS\n102: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n103: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n104: # CANONICAL STATE WRITE MECHANISM\n105: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n106: state_write_protocol:\n107:   mechanism: \"append-gateway\"\n108:   command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs --mode research --run-directory {artifact_dir} --event-json <record file>\"\n109:   applies_to: \"every append_to_jsonl and append_jsonl directive in this workflow\"\n110:   refusal_handling: \"halt on exit 2; never fall back to a direct file write\"\n111:   migration_exception: \"Embedded lifecycle writers append run-now and pause sentinel records directly; no ledger event stem exists for them yet, so the gateway would reject them.\"\n112:   exempt_append_sites: 3\n113:   contract: |\n114:     The directives below specify WHAT to record; this block specifies the mechanism. The\n115:     command accepts a canonical event envelope — a `stem` with `scope` and `data`, or an\n116:     `event_type` with a `payload` — and for this mode it also accepts a legacy-shaped row,\n117:     which it upcasts before appending. Where the upcast is lossy it returns a warning, and\n118:     the warning is surfaced rather than swallowed. Only a small number of the directives\n119:     below currently reach the log this way: of fifteen, one routes through the gateway,\n120:     six are deliberately pinned to the legacy path by the schema and refused by the\n121:     upcaster on purpose — a decision, not an omission — and the remaining eight have no\n122:     registered stem, because the ledger models research semantics and those rows are\n123:     workflow bookkeeping. Whether they should become ledger events is unsettled. A\n124:     refusal names its own reason, so the caller can tell a deliberate pin from a missing\n125:     stem. A row the upcaster refuses returns exit 1 and writes nothing, with the reason\n126:     naming why. Exit 1 is distinct from the exit 2 refusal described in the next\n127:     paragraph: exit 1 means the input never reached authority, exit 2 means authority\n128:     refused it.\n129: \n130:     The gateway authorizes the write against the mode's durable authority record, serialises it\n131:     behind the ledger fence, returns a receipt, and refreshes state_log from the ledger. Exit 0\n132:     means the record is durable. Exit 2 means it was refused, and the refusal names the check\n133:     that failed.\n134: \n135:     Writing state_log directly bypasses ordering, authorization, and the receipt. Two writers\n136:     can then interleave with no shared ordering, and a record nobody authorized carries no\n137:     receipt, so a later reader cannot tell an accepted record from an invented one. A refusal\n138:     is a halt, never a reason to write the file directly.\n139: \n140:     One exception exists and is deliberate. The embedded lifecycle writers append run-now and\n141:     pause sentinel records straight to the log, because those records have no registered event\n142:     type in this mode's ledger schema and the gateway would refuse them. They record that a\n143:     sentinel changed, not research progress. Every record the workflow itself produces goes\n144:     through the gateway, and these move to it once the schema names them.\n145: \n146:     The exempt_append_sites value is the exact number of direct-append sites covered by this\n147:     exception; any additional append site fails the conformance check until it has been\n148:     reviewed and the count deliberately raised to include it.\n149: \n150: state_paths:\n151:   # Template paths document the canonical packet layout. Runtime resolution happens via\n152:   # step_resolve_artifact_root plus the shared resolver, so root specs keep root-local\n153:   # research/ and child phases keep local research/ packet directories.\n154:   packet_dir: \"{artifact_dir}\"\n155:   config: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-research-config.json\"\n156:   state_log: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-research-state.jsonl\"\n157:   status_ledger: \"{artifact_dir}/orchestration-status.log\"\n158:   strategy: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-research-strategy.md\"\n159:   registry: \"{artifact_dir}/findings-registry.json\"\n160:   dashboard: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-research-dashboard.md\"\n161:   pause_sentinel: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-research-pause\"\n162:   run_now_sentinel: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-research-run-now\"\n163:   lock_file: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-research.lock\"\n164:   prompt_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/prompts\"\n165:   iteration_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations\"\n166:   iteration_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations/iteration-{NNN}.md\"\n167:   # Per-iteration structured delta stream (one file per iteration) — complement to the\n168:   # canonical state_log append. The delta file MUST contain at least one record whose\n169:   # `type === \"iteration\"` so the reducer can rehydrate iteration state after a partial\n170:   # run. Variants like `\"iteration_delta\"` are silently dropped by the reducer; the\n171:   # post_dispatch_validate step enforces the canonical type below.\n172:   delta_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas\"\n173:   delta_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas/iter-{NNN}.jsonl\"\n174:   research_output: \"{artifact_dir}/research.md\"\n175:   resource_map_output: \"{artifact_dir}/resource-map.md\"\n176:   archive_root: \"{artifact_archive_root}\"\n177:   synthesis_snapshot_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/synthesis-v{generation}.md\"\n178: \n179: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n180: # WORKFLOW\n181: # ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n182: workflow:\n183: \n184:   step_resolve_artifact_root:\n185:     description: \"Resolve artifact directory — use fan-out lineage override when provided, else resolve from spec_folder\"\n186:     note: \"Root specs keep research artifacts directly in {spec_folder}/research/. Child phases and sub-phases keep local packet directories in {spec_folder}/research/{packet}/, and archives stay local at {spec_folder}/research_archive/{packet}/.\"\n187:     branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n188:     if_present:\n189:       bind:\n190:         artifact_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n191:         artifact_root_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n192:         artifact_subfolder: null\n193:         artifact_archive_root: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}/_archive\"\n194:     if_absent:\n195:       command: \"node -e \\\"const { resolveArtifactRoot } = require('./.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/review-research-paths.cjs'); console.log(JSON.stringify(resolveArtifactRoot('{spec_folder}', 'research')));\\\"\"\n196:       outputs:\n197:         - artifact_root_dir: \"Resolved local research owner directory\"\n198:         - artifact_subfolder: \"Local packet subfolder ({ownerSlug}-pt-{NN}), else null\"\n199:         - artifact_dir: \"Resolved research packet directory for this target\"\n200:         - artifact_archive_root: \"Resolved local research archive directory for this target\"\n201: \n202:   step_fanout_spawn:\n203:     description: \"Spawn fan-out lineages; skip and proceed to phase_init normally when single-executor\"\n204:     skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n205:     instructions: |\n206:       Fan-out mode is active. Spawn all lineages. Each lineage runs the full loop in its own\n207:       isolated sub-packet under {artifact_dir}/lineages/{label}/.\n208:       fanout-run.cjs owns native and CLI lineage execution; native is run through the\n209:       deep/research command surface with config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir so the LEAF\n210:       deep-research agent is used only for individual iterations, never as a full-loop\n211:       sub-agent or pasted phase-running prompt.\n212:       After all lineages complete, jump directly to phase_synthesis — skip phase_init and\n213:       phase_main_loop entirely (those are the single-executor path). The merge step in\n214:       phase_synthesis will consolidate results across all lineages.\n215:     sub_steps:\n216:       step_fanout_spawn_cli:\n217:         description: \"Spawn all native and CLI lineages in capped worker pool\"\n218:         skip_when: \"no entries in config.fanout.executors\"\n219:         command: |\n220:           node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs \\\n221:             --spec-folder {spec_folder} \\\n222:             --loop-type research \\\n223:             --research-topic \"{research_topic}\" \\\n224:             --fanout-config-json '{config.fanout_json}' \\\n225:             --base-artifact-dir {artifact_dir} \\\n226:             --convergence-threshold {convergence_threshold} \\\n227:             --stop-policy {stop_policy}\n228:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n229:         wait_for_completion: true\n230: \n231:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n232:   # PHASE 1: INITIALIZATION\n233:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n234:   phase_init:\n235:     purpose: Create all state files for the research session\n236:     steps:\n237: \n238:       step_preflight_contract:\n239:         action: \"Validate required setup bindings and executable workflow contract before any file writes\"\n240:         verify:\n241:           - required_values_present: [research_topic, spec_folder, max_iterations, convergence_threshold, convergence_mode, stop_policy]\n242:           - spec_folder_is_within: \"specs/ or .opencode/specs/ (canonicalize alias roots before validation)\"\n243:           - unresolved_placeholders: \"FAIL if any user-facing template references placeholders not produced by earlier steps\"\n244:           - tool_contract: \"FAIL if executable steps reference tools outside the command allowlist\"\n245:         on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL and report the missing binding or unsupported contract reference\"\n246: \n247:       step_create_directories:\n248:         action: \"Create spec folder and research packet directories if they don't exist\"\n249:         command: \"mkdir -p {state_paths.prompt_dir} {state_paths.iteration_dir} {state_paths.delta_dir}\"\n250: \n251:       step_detect_resource_map:\n252:         action: \"Detect resource-map.md before config creation so init can persist the flag and seed Known Context\"\n253:         inspect:\n254:           - \"{spec_folder}/resource-map.md\"\n255:         classify:\n256:           present: \"resource-map.md exists at init\"\n257:           absent: \"resource-map.md does not exist at init\"\n258:         outputs:\n259:           - resource_map_present: \"Boolean true when {spec_folder}/resource-map.md exists, else false\"\n260:           - resource_map_known_context: \"When present: summarize the map by section with entry counts across READMEs, Documents, Commands, Agents, Skills, Specs, Scripts, Tests, Config, and Meta, plus a one-line theme summary for each section. When absent: 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n261: \n262:       step_resolve_canonical_names:\n263:         action: \"Resolve canonical research packet artifact names before classification\"\n264:         inspect_legacy:\n265:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/config.json\"\n266:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/state.jsonl\"\n267:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/strategy.md\"\n268:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/dashboard.md\"\n269:           - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/.pause\"\n270:         migration_policy: \"dual-read / single-write for 4 weeks\"\n271:         on_legacy_read:\n272:           append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"migration\",\"legacyPath\":\"{legacy_path}\",\"canonicalPath\":\"{canonical_path}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n273: \n274:       step_acquire_lock:\n275:         action: \"Acquire the single-writer advisory lock before session classification\"\n276:         command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs acquire --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --packet-id {spec_folder}\"\n277:         on_acquire: \"Capture ownerPid from the JSON output and reuse it for every release below. If acquired=false, fail closed — another deep-research run already holds this packet.\"\n278:         note: \"Uses the promoted runtime/ loop-lock CLI (single source of truth: stale-lock reclaim, clean owner-scoped release). macOS/BSD locking is advisory — best-effort single-writer, not a hard mutex across host calls; stale-lock override is confirm-only or explicit recovery-only.\"\n279:         # Lock-cleanup contract: the lock file MUST be released on every terminal exit path that follows acquisition.\n280:         # Runtimes honoring step_acquire_lock are required to perform this cleanup before halting or pausing.\n281:         on_halt:\n282:           action: \"Release the lock before any terminal halt branch returns control\"\n283:           applies_to: [\"step_classify_session.on_invalid_state\", \"step_classify_session.on_completed_session\", \"step_preinit_spec_branch.conflict-detected\"]\n284:           command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid}; failures here are logged but do not block the halt\"\n285:         on_cancel:\n286:           action: \"Release the lock on user cancel or pause-sentinel detection before sentinel processing\"\n287:           command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid}; cancel completes regardless of cleanup result\"\n288:         on_workflow_exit:\n289:           action: \"Release the lock as the final step of any workflow exit path (success or failure)\"\n290:           command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid}; idempotent — safe to invoke when already released\"\n291: \n292:       step_classify_session:\n293:         action: \"Classify the session before writing files\"\n294:         inspect:\n295:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n296:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n297:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n298:         classify:\n299:           fresh: \"None of the three state artifacts exist\"\n300:           resume: \"Config, JSONL, and strategy all exist and agree on topic/spec folder; missing wait-checkpoint fields are read as nextRunAt:null and remainingDelayMs:null\"\n301:           completed-session: \"Resume artifacts exist and config.status == 'complete'\"\n302:           invalid-state: \"Any partial, missing, or contradictory combination\"\n303:         outputs:\n304:           - session_state: \"fresh | resume | completed-session | invalid-state\"\n305:         on_resume:\n306:           # T-YML-DPR-01 / R50-001: Resume is a WRITE-PATH. Produces `iteration-NNN.md` + JSONL appends.\n307:           # Paired with T-DOC-03 Gate 3 trigger addition (resume, save context, save memory, /speckit:save).\n308:           gate3_classification: write-path\n309:           gate3_rationale: \"resume produces iteration-NNN.md writes and JSONL state-log appends\"\n310:           log: \"Auto-resume: state artifacts are complete and consistent. Continue the same lineage (sessionId unchanged, generation unchanged, no archive).\"\n311:           append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"resumed\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"parentSessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"lineageMode\":\"resume\",\"continuedFromRun\":{iteration_count},\"generation\":{generation},\"archivedPath\":null,\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n312:           skip_to: phase_loop\n313:         on_restart:\n314:           action: \"Archive the current research packet under the root-level research_archive/ tree and start a new lineage segment with a fresh sessionId and generation+1.\"\n315:           command: \"if [ -d {state_paths.packet_dir} ]; then mkdir -p {state_paths.archive_root} && mv {state_paths.packet_dir} {state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}; fi\"\n316:           set:\n317:             lineage_mode: \"restart\"\n318:             parent_session_id: \"{prior_session_id}\"\n319:             generation: \"{prior_generation + 1}\"\n320:           append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"restarted\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"parentSessionId\":\"{prior_session_id}\",\"lineageMode\":\"restart\",\"generation\":{generation},\"archivedPath\":\"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n321:           skip_to: step_create_config\n322:         note_deferred_branches: \"fork and completed-continue are deferred and no longer runtime-supported in this release. The reducer still reads `lineageMode` from config for dashboards and analysis, but only `new`, `resume`, and `restart` are live. See deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branch Contract for the one-session contract.\"\n323:         on_completed_session:\n324:           log: \"Prior session already completed. Do not route directly to synthesis; archive the completed research/ tree or start a fresh packet instead.\"\n325:           halt: true\n326:           message: \"Completed deep-research packet detected. Archive or replace the existing research/ tree before starting a new session.\"\n327:         on_invalid_state:\n328:           halt: true\n329:           message: \"Existing deep-research state is incomplete or contradictory. Repair or archive the invalid research packet before continuing.\"\n330:         on_fresh:\n331:           action: \"Proceed with a new session\"\n332: \n333:       step_resolve_session_id:\n334:         action: \"Resolve init session id from caller when supplied, else preserve the auto-generated fallback\"\n335:         branch_on: \"session_id\"\n336:         if_present:\n337:           bind:\n338:             session_id_init: \"{session_id}\"\n339:         if_absent:\n340:           bind:\n341:             session_id_init: \"{AUTO_SESSION_ID}\"\n342: \n343:       step_create_config:\n344:         action: \"Create deep-research-config.json from template\"\n345:         template: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-config.json\n346:         populate:\n347:           topic: \"{research_topic}\"\n348:           maxIterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n349:           minIterations: 3\n350:           # Semantic: newInfoRatio with negative-knowledge emphasis. See SKILL.md §\"Convergence Threshold Semantics\".\n351:           convergenceThreshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n352:           antiConvergence.convergenceMode: \"{convergence_mode}\"\n353:           antiConvergence.divergent: {}\n354:           stuckThreshold: 3\n355:           minIdeaObservations: 2\n356:           maxDurationMinutes: 120\n357:           specFolder: \"{spec_folder}\"\n358:           resource_map_present: \"{resource_map_present}\"\n359:           # Honor the parsed --no-resource-map flag from deep-research.md:73 (default true; false when flag is set).\n360:           # The markdown command parses $ARGUMENTS and binds {resource_map_emit} before this step runs.\n361:           resource_map.emit: \"{resource_map_emit}\"\n362:           createdAt: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n363:           status: \"initialized\"\n364:           executionMode: \"auto\"\n365:           lineage.sessionId: \"{session_id_init}\"\n366:           lineage.parentSessionId: null\n367:           lineage.lineageMode: \"new\"\n368:           lineage.generation: 1\n369:           lineage.continuedFromRun: null\n370:           nextRunAt: null\n371:           remainingDelayMs: null\n372:         output: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n373: \n374:       step_create_state_log:\n375:         action: \"Initialize JSONL state log with config record\"\n376:         # Same parsed --no-resource-map flag honored here so config and state_log agree from line 1.\n377:         content: '{\"type\":\"config\",\"topic\":\"{research_topic}\",\"maxIterations\":{max_iterations},\"minIterations\":3,\"convergenceThreshold\":{convergence_threshold},\"antiConvergence\":{\"convergenceMode\":\"{convergence_mode}\",\"divergent\":{}},\"minIdeaObservations\":2,\"resource_map_present\":{resource_map_present},\"resource_map\":{\"emit\":{resource_map_emit}},\"createdAt\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"specFolder\":\"{spec_folder}\",\"nextRunAt\":null,\"remainingDelayMs\":null}'\n378:         output: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n379: \n380:       step_create_strategy:\n381:         action: \"Create strategy file from template with initial questions\"\n382:         template: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md\n383:         populate:\n384:           topic: \"{research_topic}\"\n385:           key_questions: \"Derive 3-5 key questions from the research topic\"\n386:           known_context: \"None\"\n387:           known_context_summary: \"None\"\n388:           max_iterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n389:           convergence_threshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n390:         output: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n391: \n392:       step_create_registry:\n393:         action: \"Initialize reducer-owned findings registry\"\n394:         content: '{\"openQuestions\":[],\"resolvedQuestions\":[],\"keyFindings\":[],\"ruledOutDirections\":[],\"metrics\":{\"iterationsCompleted\":0,\"openQuestions\":0,\"resolvedQuestions\":0,\"keyFindings\":0,\"convergenceScore\":0,\"coverageBySources\":{}}}'\n395:         output: \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n396: \n397:       step_enrich_strategy_context:\n398:         action: \"Ensure Known Context is written only after strategy.md exists\"\n399:         condition: \"prior_context_found\"\n400:         edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n401:         note: \"Append or replace the Known Context section with prior_context_summary and retained detail from prior_context\"\n402: \n403:       step_enrich_strategy_resource_map:\n404:         action: \"Inject resource-map status into Known Context after strategy.md exists\"\n405:         edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n406:         note: \"When resource_map_present is true, append the resource_map_known_context snapshot. When false, append 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n407: \n408:       step_detect_spec_present:\n409:         action: \"Classify late-INIT spec.md state after the durable research packet exists\"\n410:         inspect:\n411:           - \"{spec_folder}/spec.md\"\n412:           - \"{state_paths.lock_file}\"\n413:         classify:\n414:           no-spec: \"spec.md is absent before any pre-init mutation\"\n415:           spec-present: \"spec.md exists and approved host anchors are available for bounded mutation\"\n416:           spec-just-created-by-this-run: \"spec.md already carries this run's DR seed markers and should not be reseeded\"\n417:           conflict-detected: \"missing host anchor, duplicate markers, or generated-block ambiguity makes mutation unsafe\"\n418:         outputs:\n419:           - folder_state: \"no-spec | spec-present | spec-just-created-by-this-run | conflict-detected\"\n420:           - normalized_topic: \"Trim, lowercase, and collapse whitespace in research_topic before dedupe checks\"\n421:         append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"spec_check_result\",\"folder_state\":\"{folder_state}\",\"normalized_topic\":\"{normalized_topic}\",\"specPath\":\"{spec_folder}/spec.md\",\"lockPath\":\"{state_paths.lock_file}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n422: \n423:       step_preinit_spec_branch:\n424:         action: \"Run the bounded pre-init spec branch required by spec_check_protocol\"\n425:         protocol_reference: \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md\"\n426:         branches:\n427:           no-spec:\n428:             create: \"{spec_folder}/spec.md\"\n429:             seed_markers:\n430:               - \"<!-- DR-SEED:REQUIREMENTS -->\"\n431:               - \"<!-- DR-SEED:SCOPE -->\"\n432:             requirements_host: \"Seed Requirements from the research ask without broadening scope\"\n433:             scope_host: \"Seed Scope from the research ask without inventing implementation details\"\n434:             set:\n435:               folder_state: \"spec-just-created-by-this-run\"\n436:               validate_spec_doc: true\n437:             append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"spec_mutation\",\"event\":\"spec_seed_created\",\"folder_state\":\"spec-just-created-by-this-run\",\"anchors_touched\":[\"Requirements\",\"Scope\"],\"diff_summary\":\"Seeded Level 1 spec.md from research topic with DR seed markers.\",\"seed_markers\":[\"DR-SEED:REQUIREMENTS\",\"DR-SEED:SCOPE\"],\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n438:           spec-present:\n439:             edit: \"{spec_folder}/spec.md\"\n440:             set:\n441:               validate_spec_doc: true\n442:             idempotency_check:\n443:               host_anchor: \"Open Questions\"\n444:               normalized_match: \"Normalize the existing anchor text by lowercasing, stripping punctuation, collapsing whitespace, and trimming before comparing with {normalized_topic}.\"\n445:               if_match:\n446:                 skip_append: true\n447:                 append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"spec_mutation\",\"event\":\"spec_preinit_context_deduped\",\"folder_state\":\"spec-present\",\"anchors_touched\":[\"Open Questions\"],\"diff_summary\":\"Skipped duplicate pre-init topic append because normalized topic already exists in Open Questions.\",\"normalized_topic\":\"{normalized_topic}\",\"specPath\":\"{spec_folder}/spec.md\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n448:               if_no_match:\n449:                 append_only:\n450:                   - host_anchor: \"Open Questions\"\n451:                     content: \"Add the normalized research topic only if it is not already present.\"\n452:                   - host_anchor: \"Research Context\"\n453:                     content: \"Add a bounded note that deep-research is active for this topic and that research/research.md remains canonical.\"\n454:                 append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"spec_mutation\",\"event\":\"spec_preinit_context_added\",\"folder_state\":\"spec-present\",\"anchors_touched\":[\"Open Questions\",\"Research Context\"],\"diff_summary\":\"Appended bounded pre-init research context for the normalized topic.\",\"normalized_topic\":\"{normalized_topic}\",\"specPath\":\"{spec_folder}/spec.md\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n455:           spec-just-created-by-this-run:\n456:             verify_markers:\n457:               - \"<!-- DR-SEED:REQUIREMENTS -->\"\n458:               - \"<!-- DR-SEED:SCOPE -->\"\n459:             set:\n460:               validate_spec_doc: false\n461:             note: \"Treat already-seeded spec.md as a no-op guard and continue.\"\n462:           conflict-detected:\n463:             append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"spec_mutation\",\"event\":\"spec_mutation_conflict\",\"folder_state\":\"conflict-detected\",\"reason\":\"Pre-init spec.md mutation is ambiguous or unsafe.\",\"specPath\":\"{spec_folder}/spec.md\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n464:             halt: true\n465: \n466:       step_validate_preinit_spec_doc:\n467:         action: \"Run targeted strict validation after any deep-research pre-init spec.md mutation\"\n468:         condition: \"validate_spec_doc\"\n469:         command: \"SPECKIT_RULES=FRONTMATTER_VALID,LEVEL_DECLARED,TEMPLATE_SOURCE,TEMPLATE_HEADERS,PLACEHOLDER_FILLED,ANCHORS_VALID,SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY,TOC_POLICY bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh {spec_folder} --strict\"\n470:         note: \"This enforces the authored-spec markdown structural contract without applying full-packet required-file or completeness checks to workflow-owned research artifacts. It uses the Node validation orchestrator, whose strict path was measured at about 108ms for a fresh Level 3 packet on the local harness.\"\n471: \n472:       step_telemetry_heartbeat_started:\n473:         action: \"Emit a single-loop started row in the orchestration status ledger\"\n474:         skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n475:         canonical_lifecycle_event: \"iteration_start\"\n476:         command: |\n477:           node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n478:           import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n479: \n480:           import { appendJsonlIfChangedAtomic } from './.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/atomic-state.ts';\n481:           import observabilityEvents from './.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/observability-events.cjs';\n482: \n483:           const { appendObservabilityEvent } = observabilityEvents;\n484:           const config = JSON.parse(readFileSync('{state_paths.config}', 'utf8'));\n485:           const timestamp = '{ISO_8601_NOW}';\n486:           const sessionId = String(config.lineage?.sessionId ?? '{AUTO_SESSION_ID}');\n487:           const generation = Number(config.lineage?.generation ?? 1);\n488:           const observabilityPath = '{state_paths.packet_dir}/observability-events.jsonl';\n489:           const row = {\n490:             event: 'started',\n491:             label: 'single',\n492:             at: timestamp,\n493:             duration_ms: 0,\n494:             loop_type: 'research',\n495:             sessionId,\n496:             generation,\n497:             gauges: { iterations: 0, elapsed_ms: 0, score: 0 },\n498:           };\n499: \n500:           const appended = appendJsonlIfChangedAtomic('{state_paths.status_ledger}', row, {\n501:             diffData: { event: row.event, label: row.label, sessionId, generation, gauges: { iterations: 0, score: 0 } },\n502:             diffField: 'state_hash',\n503:           });\n504:           if (appended) {\n505:             try {\n506:               appendObservabilityEvent(observabilityPath, row, {\n507:                 producer: 'deep-research-auto',\n508:                 stream: 'single-loop-telemetry',\n509:                 subject: { label: row.label, sessionId, generation },\n510:                 event: row.event,\n511:                 status: 'running',\n512:               });\n513:             } catch {}\n514:           }\n515:           EOF\n516:         working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n517:         outputs:\n518:           - status_ledger_started: \"A fan-out-shaped status row with label single and event started\"\n519: \n520:       step_init_complete:\n521:         log: \"Initialization complete. Config, state, and strategy files created.\"\n522:         set: { current_iteration: 1, current_segment: 1, stuck_count: 0 }\n523: \n524:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n525:   # PHASE 2: ITERATION LOOP\n526:   # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n527:   phase_loop:\n528:     purpose: Dispatch agent iterations until convergence\n529:     repeat: true\n530:     max_repeats: \"{max_iterations}\"\n531:     steps:\n532: \n533:       step_read_state:\n534:         action: \"Read current state from JSONL and strategy\"\n535:         read:\n536:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n537:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n538:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n539:         extract:\n540:           - iteration_count: \"Count lines where type === 'iteration'\"\n541:           - current_iteration: \"iteration_count + 1\"\n542:           - current_segment: \"Latest segment_start event segment, else 1\"\n543:           - last_newInfoRatio: \"Extract newInfoRatio from last iteration record\"\n544:           - last_focus: \"Extract focus from latest iteration record, else 'none yet'\"\n545:           - ratio_prev: \"Extract newInfoRatio from second-latest iteration record, else 'N/A'\"\n546:           - ratio_latest: \"Extract newInfoRatio from latest iteration record, else 'N/A'\"\n547:           - next_focus: \"Extract 'Next Focus' section from strategy.md\"\n548:           - remaining_questions: \"Count unchecked items in 'Key Questions'\"\n549:           - remaining_questions_list: \"List unchecked key questions from strategy.md\"\n550:           - carried_forward_open_questions: \"Extract 'Carried-Forward Open Questions' section from strategy.md, else '[None yet]'\"\n551:           - answered_count: \"Count answered questions from strategy.md\"\n552:           - total_questions: \"Count total questions tracked in strategy.md\"\n553:           - resource_map_present: \"Extract boolean from deep-research-config.json, default false\"\n554:           - resource_map_prompt_line: \"If resource_map_present is true, return 'Resource map: prior-inventoried files are listed in {spec_folder}/resource-map.md; treat them as the exclusion set when hunting for net-new files; flag only missed-from-map candidates as gaps.' Else return 'Resource map: resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate.'\"\n555:           - lineage_context_prompt_line: \"If a refreshed lineage context summary exists from the previous iteration, return 'Lineage context refresh: {summary}'. Else use prior_context_summary from startup when available; otherwise return 'Lineage context refresh: none loaded yet.'\"\n556:           - least_explored: \"First unanswered question not covered by the most recent iteration focus, else first unanswered question\"\n557:           - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records as 'run N: focus (ratio)'\"\n558:           - latest_status: \"Extract status from latest iteration record, else 'none yet'\"\n559:           - nextRunAt: \"Extract nullable nextRunAt from deep-research-config.json, default null\"\n560:           - remainingDelayMs: \"Extract nullable remainingDelayMs from deep-research-config.json, default null\"\n561:           - min_iterations_present: \"Boolean true when deep-research-config.json has a numeric minIterations field\"\n562:           - min_iterations_missing_warning: \"Boolean true when minIterations is missing; use no floor and log a warning so older configs keep prior stop behavior\"\n563:           - min_iterations_raw: \"Extract numeric minIterations from deep-research-config.json when present, default 0\"\n564:           - effective_min_iterations: \"Clamp min_iterations_raw to the inclusive range 0..max_iterations; if min_iterations_raw exceeds max_iterations, use max_iterations\"\n565:           - min_iterations_clamped: \"Boolean true when min_iterations_raw > max_iterations\"\n566:           - min_iterations_guard_already_passed: \"Boolean true when state_log already contains event == 'min_iterations_guard_pass'\"\n567:           - convergence_mode: \"Extract antiConvergence.convergenceMode when it is one of 'default', 'off', 'sliding-window', or 'divergent'; default to 'default'\"\n568:           - convergence_mode_warning: \"Boolean true when antiConvergence.convergenceMode is present with an unsupported value; use 'default'\"\n569:           - rejected_patterns_count: \"Read registry.rejectedPatterns length when registry exists, else 0\"\n570:           - rejected_candidate_matches: \"Read registry.suppressedCandidates when registry exists, else []\"\n571:           - rejected_pattern_fuzzy_threshold: \"Read config.rejectedPatternFuzzyThreshold when present, else 0.85\"\n572:           - min_idea_observations: \"Read config.minIdeaObservations when present, default 2; clamp to 1..10\"\n573:           - observed_ideas_count: \"Read registry.observedIdeas length when registry exists, else 0\"\n574:           - promoted_ideas_count: \"Read registry.promotedIdeas length when registry exists, else 0\"\n575:           - promoted_ideas_list: \"Read registry.promotedIdeas idea text in rank order when registry exists, else []\"\n576:           - suppressed_ideas_count: \"Read registry.suppressedIdeas length when registry exists, else 0\"\n577:           - pivot_lineage: \"Summarize registry.divergence.completed and registry.divergence.overrides with pivot ids, source iterations, and selected focus; else 'none yet'\"\n578:           - saturated_directions: \"List registry.divergence.saturatedDirections; else 'none yet'\"\n579: \n580:       step_run_now_check:\n581:         action: \"Detect and consume a one-shot run-now sentinel before pause/convergence/dispatch\"\n582:         command: |\n583:           node <<'EOF'\n584:           const { appendFileSync, existsSync, renameSync, unlinkSync } = require('node:fs');\n585: \n586:           const stateLogPath = \"{state_paths.state_log}\";\n587:           const sentinelPath = \"{state_paths.run_now_sentinel}\";\n588:           const pausePath = \"{state_paths.pause_sentinel}\";\n589:           const timestamp = \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\";\n590:           const sessionId = \"{config.lineage.sessionId}\";\n591:           const generation = Number(\"{config.lineage.generation}\");\n592:           const run = Number(\"{current_iteration}\");\n593: \n594:           function append(event) {\n595:             appendFileSync(\n596:               stateLogPath,\n597:               `${JSON.stringify({\n598:                 type: \"event\",\n599:                 mode: \"research\",\n600:                 run,\n601:                 timestamp,\n602:                 sessionId,\n603:                 generation,\n604:                 ...event,\n605:               })}\\n`,\n606:               \"utf8\",\n607:             );\n608:           }\n609: \n610:           if (existsSync(sentinelPath)) {\n611:             append({ event: \"run_now_requested\", sentinelPath });\n612:             if (existsSync(pausePath)) {\n613:               append({\n614:                 event: \"run_now_rejected\",\n615:                 reason: \"loop_paused\",\n616:                 sentinelPath,\n617:                 pauseSentinelPath: pausePath,\n618:               });\n619:             } else {\n620:               const claimPath = `${sentinelPath}.consuming.${process.pid}.${Date.now()}`;\n621:               try {\n622:                 renameSync(sentinelPath, claimPath);\n623:                 unlinkSync(claimPath);\n624:                 append({\n625:                   event: \"run_now_accepted\",\n626:                   sentinelPath,\n627:                   dispatchEvent: \"iteration_start\",\n628:                 });\n629:               } catch (error) {\n630:                 if (!error || error.code !== \"ENOENT\") {\n631:                   throw error;\n632:                 }\n633:               }\n634:             }\n635:           }\n636:           EOF\n637:         outputs:\n638:           - run_now_requested: \"Emitted when {state_paths.run_now_sentinel} exists at the loop boundary\"\n639:           - run_now_accepted: \"Emitted after the sentinel is atomically renamed and deleted before dispatch\"\n640:           - run_now_rejected: \"Emitted with reason loop_paused when pause takes precedence; sentinel remains present\"\n641: \n642:       step_check_pause_sentinel:\n643:         action: \"Check for pause sentinel file\"\n644:         check: \"Does {state_paths.pause_sentinel} exist?\"\n645:         if_exists:\n646:           log_event: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"userPaused\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"stopReason\":\"userPaused\",\"sentinelPath\":\"{state_paths.pause_sentinel}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n647:           message: \"Research paused. Delete research/.deep-research-pause to resume.\"\n648:           halt: true\n649:         if_not_exists:\n650:           proceed: true\n651: \n652:       step_validate_convergence_config:\n653:         action: \"Validate convergence floor settings when loading config\"\n654:         if_min_iterations_missing:\n655:           append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"config_warning\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"field\":\"minIterations\",\"fallback\":0,\"message\":\"minIterations missing; using no convergence floor for backward compatibility.\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n656:           log: \"minIterations missing; using no convergence floor for backward compatibility.\"\n657:         if_min_iterations_clamped:\n658:           append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"config_warning\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"field\":\"minIterations\",\"configured\":{min_iterations_raw},\"effective\":{effective_min_iterations},\"maxIterations\":{max_iterations},\"message\":\"minIterations exceeds maxIterations; clamping to the hard cap.\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n659:           log: \"minIterations exceeds maxIterations; clamping to the hard cap.\"\n660:         if_convergence_mode_invalid:\n661:           append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"config_warning\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"field\":\"convergenceMode\",\"fallback\":\"default\",\"message\":\"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n662:           log: \"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\"\n663: \n664:       step_graph_convergence:\n665:         action: \"Evaluate coverage-graph convergence before the inline 3-signal vote and persist the graph decision snapshot\"\n666:         bash: 'node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type \"research\" --session-id \"{config.lineage.sessionId}\" --convergence-mode \"{convergence_mode}\" --persist-snapshot --iteration \"{current_iteration}\"'\n667:         note: \"Run before the inline vote. STOP from the inline 3-signal vote is allowed only when the graph decision is STOP_ALLOWED or absent.\"\n668:         outputs:\n669:           - graph_decision: \"Tool decision value (CONTINUE | STOP_ALLOWED | STOP_BLOCKED), else null when unavailable\"\n670:           - graph_decision_json: \"JSON-encoded graph decision string, else null\"\n671:           - graph_signals_json: \"Tool signals object, else {}\"\n672:           - graph_blockers_json: \"Tool blockers array, else []\"\n673:           - graph_trace_json: \"Tool trace payload, else []\"\n674:           - graph_convergence_score: \"signals.blendedScore when present, else the best available graph score, else 0\"\n675:         append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"graph_convergence\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"decision\":{graph_decision_json},\"signals\":{graph_signals_json},\"blockers\":{graph_blockers_json},\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n676: \n677:       step_check_convergence:\n678:         action: \"Evaluate stop conditions and combine the inline 3-signal vote with graph convergence\"\n679:         algorithm: |\n680:           1. if iteration_count >= max_iterations: STOP (maxIterationsReached). This terminal cap bypasses quality-guard overrides; record failed guards/blockers as synthesis evidence instead of continuing.\n681:           2. if stuck_count >= config.stuckThreshold: STUCK_RECOVERY\n682:           3. if convergence_mode == \"off\": skip convergence stop candidates and continue unless a terminal cap, pause sentinel, or recovery halt has already fired.\n683:           4. if remaining_questions == 0: STOP (all_questions_answered)\n684:           5. GRAPH-ASSISTED COMPOSITE CONVERGENCE:\n685:                step_graph_convergence already recorded graph_decision, graph_signals_json, graph_blockers_json, and graph_convergence_score for this run.\n686:                The existing inline 3-signal vote still computes the inline STOP candidate and is not replaced.\n687:                signals = []\n688:                Filter: exclude iterations where status == thought from signal inputs (use only evidence iterations)\n689:                a) Rolling average (w=0.30, needs 3+ iterations):\n690:                   avg = mean(last 3 newInfoRatios)\n691:                   stop if avg < convergence_threshold\n692:                b) MAD noise floor (w=0.35, needs 4+ iterations):\n693:                   noiseFloor = MAD(all ratios) * 1.4826\n694:                   stop if latest ratio <= noiseFloor\n695:                c) Question entropy (w=0.35):\n696:                   coverage = answered / total questions\n697:                   stop if coverage >= 0.85\n698:                Redistribute weights for unavailable signals.\n699:                if weighted_stop_score > 0.60: inline_stop_candidate = true\n700:                Combined stop rule: STOP only if the inline 3-signal vote says STOP AND graph_decision is STOP_ALLOWED or absent.\n701:                if inline_stop_candidate and graph_decision == \"STOP_BLOCKED\":\n702:                  decision = \"BLOCKED\"\n703:                  reason = \"blockedStop\"\n704:                  stop_blocked = true\n705:                  blocked_by_json = JSON array derived from graph_blockers_json\n706:                  blocked_by_csv = comma-separated blocker names derived from graph_blockers_json\n707:                  gate_convergence_pass = false\n708:                  gate_convergence_score = graph_convergence_score\n709:                  gate_key_question_coverage_pass = no blocker named questionCoverage\n710:                  gate_evidence_density_pass = no blocker named sourceDiversity or evidenceDepth\n711:                  gate_evidence_density_sources = graph_signals_json.sourceDiversity or 0\n712:                  gate_hotspot_saturation_pass = true\n713:                  recovery_strategy = first blocker reason/message, else \"Collect deeper graph evidence before stopping.\"\n714:                else if inline_stop_candidate and (graph_decision == \"STOP_ALLOWED\" or graph_decision is absent):\n715:                  decision = \"STOP\"\n716:                  reason = \"composite_converged\"\n717:                  stop_blocked = false\n718:           6. else: CONTINUE\n719:           7. if decision == \"STOP\" and reason != \"maxIterationsReached\" and effective_min_iterations > 1 and iteration_count < effective_min_iterations:\n720:                decision = \"CONTINUE\"\n721:                reason = \"minIterationsNotReached\"\n722:                min_iterations_guard_blocked = true\n723:                min_iterations_guard_pass = false\n\n(Output capped at 50 KB. Showing lines 1-723. Use offset=724 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# DEEP RESEARCH: AUTONOMOUS DEEP RESEARCH LOOP (AUTO MODE)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# YAML PREDICATE GRAMMAR CONTRACT (S7 / M11):\n# - This asset does not currently use typed BooleanExpr predicates under\n#   `when:`; flow control is branch-label-driven (`on_resume`, `on_fresh`,\n#   `on_restart`, etc.). Retain the existing shape.\n# - `after:` carries prose timing / narrative notes if needed; `when:` in\n#   this file is reserved for future typed predicates and must NOT carry\n#   free-form narrative prose.\n# - See `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/predicates/boolean-expr.ts`\n#   for the canonical BooleanExpr grammar.\n#\n# GATE 3 CLASSIFICATION (T-YML-DPR-01 / paired with T-DOC-03 R50-001):\n# - `resume` is a tested WRITE-PATH that produces `iteration-NNN.md` files\n#   and JSONL state-log appends. The workflow classifies resume as\n#   write-path below (see `gate3_classification` fields) so Gate 3 trigger\n#   extraction can surface resume correctly rather than false-negative.\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nrole: Deep Research Loop Manager","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml","text":"# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# DEEP RESEARCH: AUTONOMOUS DEEP RESEARCH LOOP (AUTO MODE)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# YAML PREDICATE GRAMMAR CONTRACT (S7 / M11):\n# - This asset does not currently use typed BooleanExpr predicates under\n#   `when:`; flow control is branch-label-driven (`on_resume`, `on_fresh`,\n#   `on_restart`, etc.). Retain the existing shape.\n# - `after:` carries prose timing / narrative notes if needed; `when:` in\n#   this file is reserved for future typed predicates and must NOT carry\n#   free-form narrative prose.\n# - See `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/predicates/boolean-expr.ts`\n#   for the canonical BooleanExpr grammar.\n#\n# GATE 3 CLASSIFICATION (T-YML-DPR-01 / paired with T-DOC-03 R50-001):\n# - `resume` is a tested WRITE-PATH that produces `iteration-NNN.md` files\n#   and JSONL state-log appends. The workflow classifies resume as\n#   write-path below (see `gate3_classification` fields) so Gate 3 trigger\n#   extraction can surface resume correctly rather than false-negative.\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nrole: Deep Research Loop Manager\npurpose: Iterative deep research with convergence detection\naction: Run deep-research loop from initialization through synthesis\noperating_mode:\n  workflow: iterative_loop\n  workflow_compliance: MANDATORY\n  workflow_execution: autonomous\n  approvals: none\n  tracking: progressive_research_state\n  validation: convergence_detection\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# OPERATING PRINCIPLES\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\noperating_principles:\n  core: \"Fresh context per iteration + externalized state = no context degradation\"\n  approach: \"Dispatch focused agent, evaluate convergence, repeat or stop\"\n  mandate: \"Never hold findings in memory; write everything to files\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# USER INPUTS (from setup phase)\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nuser_inputs:\n  research_topic: \"[RESEARCH_TOPIC] - Topic to investigate deeply. REQUIRED.\"\n  spec_folder: \"[SPEC_FOLDER] - Spec folder path. REQUIRED.\"\n  max_iterations: \"[MAX_ITERATIONS] - Maximum loop iterations. Default: 10.\"\n  convergence_threshold: \"[CONVERGENCE_THRESHOLD] - Stop threshold. Default: 0.05.\"\n  convergence_mode: \"[default|off|sliding-window|divergent] - Convergence policy modifier. Default: default.\"\n  stop_policy: \"[convergence|max-iterations] - Convergence stop policy; max-iterations forces the loop to run every iteration. Default: convergence.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# CONTEXT LOADING\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\ncontext_loading:\n  trigger: \"At workflow START, before phase_init\"\n  purpose: \"Load prior research context for the topic and buffer it until strategy.md exists\"\n  retrieval:\n    mechanism: \"continuity-ladder-then-ripgrep\"\n    note: \"File reads only. Nothing here needs a running daemon, and every step is reproducible by hand.\"\n    ladder:\n      - \"{spec_folder}/handover.md when present\"\n      - \"the _memory.continuity frontmatter block in {spec_folder}/implementation-summary.md\"\n      - \"the packet's canonical spec docs, spec.md and decision-record.md, for what the first two steps leave open\"\n    free_text_recipe: \"rg --no-config --json --fixed-strings --ignore-case -C 2 --glob '*.md' --glob '!**/z_archive/**' --glob '!**/node_modules/**' -- '{research_topic}' specs .opencode\"\n    recipe_contract: \".opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/references/retrieval/retrieval-conventions.md\"\n    exit_status: \"0 is a hit set, 1 is a clean no-hit, 2 or higher is a failure that must be surfaced instead of reported as no-hit\"\n    ranking: \"Ripgrep does not rank. Order the hits caller-side with the tuple in retrieval-conventions.md section 5.\"\n  when_to_skip: [\"User says 'skip context' or 'fresh start'\"]\n  behavior:\n    if_context_found: \"Store full results as prior_context plus a concise prior_context_summary; inject after strategy.md is created.\"\n    if_no_context: \"Set prior_context and prior_context_summary to 'None' and continue.\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# SKILL REFERENCE\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nskill_reference:\n  skill: system-deep-loop\n  skill_md: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/SKILL.md\n  references:\n    loop_protocol: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md\n    spec_check_protocol: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md\n    state_format: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/state/state-format.md\n    convergence: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/convergence/convergence.md\n  templates:\n    config: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-config.json\n    strategy: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# AGENT CONFIGURATION\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nagent_config:\n  agent: deep-research\n  agent_file: \".opencode/agents/deep-research.md\"\n  # Canonical path. Runtime-specific directories (e.g. .claude/agents/) reference this source.\n  model: opus\n  leaf_only: true\n  tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Grep, Glob, WebFetch]\n  mcp_servers: []\n  tool_call_budget: { target: 8, max: 12 }\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# STATE FILE PATHS\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# CANONICAL STATE WRITE MECHANISM\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nstate_write_protocol:\n  mechanism: \"append-gateway\"\n  command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs --mode research --run-directory {artifact_dir} --event-json <record file>\"\n  applies_to: \"every append_to_jsonl and append_jsonl directive in this workflow\"\n  refusal_handling: \"halt on exit 2; never fall back to a direct file write\"\n  migration_exception: \"Embedded lifecycle writers append run-now and pause sentinel records directly; no ledger event stem exists for them yet, so the gateway would reject them.\"\n  exempt_append_sites: 3\n  contract: |\n    The directives below specify WHAT to record; this block specifies the mechanism. The\n    command accepts a canonical event envelope — a `stem` with `scope` and `data`, or an\n    `event_type` with a `payload` — and for this mode it also accepts a legacy-shaped row,\n    which it upcasts before appending. Where the upcast is lossy it returns a warning, and\n    the warning is surfaced rather than swallowed. Only a small number of the directives\n    below currently reach the log this way: of fifteen, one routes through the gateway,\n    six are deliberately pinned to the legacy path by the schema and refused by the\n    upcaster on purpose — a decision, not an omission — and the remaining eight have no\n    registered stem, because the ledger models research semantics and those rows are\n    workflow bookkeeping. Whether they should become ledger events is unsettled. A\n    refusal names its own reason, so the caller can tell a deliberate pin from a missing\n    stem. A row the upcaster refuses returns exit 1 and writes nothing, with the reason\n    naming why. Exit 1 is distinct from the exit 2 refusal described in the next\n    paragraph: exit 1 means the input never reached authority, exit 2 means authority\n    refused it.\n\n    The gateway authorizes the write against the mode's durable authority record, serialises it\n    behind the ledger fence, returns a receipt, and refreshes state_log from the ledger. Exit 0\n    means the record is durable. Exit 2 means it was refused, and the refusal names the check\n    that failed.\n\n    Writing state_log directly bypasses ordering, authorization, and the receipt. Two writers\n    can then interleave with no shared ordering, and a record nobody authorized carries no\n    receipt, so a later reader cannot tell an accepted record from an invented one. A refusal\n    is a halt, never a reason to write the file directly.\n\n    One exception exists and is deliberate. The embedded lifecycle writers append run-now and\n    pause sentinel records straight to the log, because those records have no registered event\n    type in this mode's ledger schema and the gateway would refuse them. They record that a\n    sentinel changed, not research progress. Every record the workflow itself produces goes\n    through the gateway, and these move to it once the schema names them.\n\n    The exempt_append_sites value is the exact number of direct-append sites covered by this\n    exception; any additional append site fails the conformance check until it has been\n    reviewed and the count deliberately raised to include it.\n\nstate_paths:\n  # Template paths document the canonical packet layout. Runtime resolution happens via\n  # step_resolve_artifact_root plus the shared resolver, so root specs keep root-local\n  # research/ and child phases keep local research/ packet directories.\n  packet_dir: \"{artifact_dir}\"\n  config: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-research-config.json\"\n  state_log: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-research-state.jsonl\"\n  status_ledger: \"{artifact_dir}/orchestration-status.log\"\n  strategy: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-research-strategy.md\"\n  registry: \"{artifact_dir}/findings-registry.json\"\n  dashboard: \"{artifact_dir}/deep-research-dashboard.md\"\n  pause_sentinel: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-research-pause\"\n  run_now_sentinel: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-research-run-now\"\n  lock_file: \"{artifact_dir}/.deep-research.lock\"\n  prompt_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/prompts\"\n  iteration_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations\"\n  iteration_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/iterations/iteration-{NNN}.md\"\n  # Per-iteration structured delta stream (one file per iteration) — complement to the\n  # canonical state_log append. The delta file MUST contain at least one record whose\n  # `type === \"iteration\"` so the reducer can rehydrate iteration state after a partial\n  # run. Variants like `\"iteration_delta\"` are silently dropped by the reducer; the\n  # post_dispatch_validate step enforces the canonical type below.\n  delta_dir: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas\"\n  delta_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/deltas/iter-{NNN}.jsonl\"\n  research_output: \"{artifact_dir}/research.md\"\n  resource_map_output: \"{artifact_dir}/resource-map.md\"\n  archive_root: \"{artifact_archive_root}\"\n  synthesis_snapshot_pattern: \"{artifact_dir}/synthesis-v{generation}.md\"\n\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n# WORKFLOW\n# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nworkflow:\n\n  step_resolve_artifact_root:\n    description: \"Resolve artifact directory — use fan-out lineage override when provided, else resolve from spec_folder\"\n    note: \"Root specs keep research artifacts directly in {spec_folder}/research/. Child phases and sub-phases keep local packet directories in {spec_folder}/research/{packet}/, and archives stay local at {spec_folder}/research_archive/{packet}/.\"\n    branch_on: \"config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\"\n    if_present:\n      bind:\n        artifact_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n        artifact_root_dir: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}\"\n        artifact_subfolder: null\n        artifact_archive_root: \"{config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir}/_archive\"\n    if_absent:\n      command: \"node -e \\\"const { resolveArtifactRoot } = require('./.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/shared/review-research-paths.cjs'); console.log(JSON.stringify(resolveArtifactRoot('{spec_folder}', 'research')));\\\"\"\n      outputs:\n        - artifact_root_dir: \"Resolved local research owner directory\"\n        - artifact_subfolder: \"Local packet subfolder ({ownerSlug}-pt-{NN}), else null\"\n        - artifact_dir: \"Resolved research packet directory for this target\"\n        - artifact_archive_root: \"Resolved local research archive directory for this target\"\n\n  step_fanout_spawn:\n    description: \"Spawn fan-out lineages; skip and proceed to phase_init normally when single-executor\"\n    skip_when: \"config.fanout is absent\"\n    instructions: |\n      Fan-out mode is active. Spawn all lineages. Each lineage runs the full loop in its own\n      isolated sub-packet under {artifact_dir}/lineages/{label}/.\n      fanout-run.cjs owns native and CLI lineage execution; native is run through the\n      deep/research command surface with config.fanout_lineage_artifact_dir so the LEAF\n      deep-research agent is used only for individual iterations, never as a full-loop\n      sub-agent or pasted phase-running prompt.\n      After all lineages complete, jump directly to phase_synthesis — skip phase_init and\n      phase_main_loop entirely (those are the single-executor path). The merge step in\n      phase_synthesis will consolidate results across all lineages.\n    sub_steps:\n      step_fanout_spawn_cli:\n        description: \"Spawn all native and CLI lineages in capped worker pool\"\n        skip_when: \"no entries in config.fanout.executors\"\n        command: |\n          node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs \\\n            --spec-folder {spec_folder} \\\n            --loop-type research \\\n            --research-topic \"{research_topic}\" \\\n            --fanout-config-json '{config.fanout_json}' \\\n            --base-artifact-dir {artifact_dir} \\\n            --convergence-threshold {convergence_threshold} \\\n            --stop-policy {stop_policy}\n        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n        wait_for_completion: true\n\n  # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n  # PHASE 1: INITIALIZATION\n  # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n  phase_init:\n    purpose: Create all state files for the research session\n    steps:\n\n      step_preflight_contract:\n        action: \"Validate required setup bindings and executable workflow contract before any file writes\"\n        verify:\n          - required_values_present: [research_topic, spec_folder, max_iterations, convergence_threshold, convergence_mode, stop_policy]\n          - spec_folder_is_within: \"specs/ or .opencode/specs/ (canonicalize alias roots before validation)\"\n          - unresolved_placeholders: \"FAIL if any user-facing template references placeholders not produced by earlier steps\"\n          - tool_contract: \"FAIL if executable steps reference tools outside the command allowlist\"\n        on_fail: \"Halt with STATUS=FAIL and report the missing binding or unsupported contract reference\"\n\n      step_create_directories:\n        action: \"Create spec folder and research packet directories if they don't exist\"\n        command: \"mkdir -p {state_paths.prompt_dir} {state_paths.iteration_dir} {state_paths.delta_dir}\"\n\n      step_detect_resource_map:\n        action: \"Detect resource-map.md before config creation so init can persist the flag and seed Known Context\"\n        inspect:\n          - \"{spec_folder}/resource-map.md\"\n        classify:\n          present: \"resource-map.md exists at init\"\n          absent: \"resource-map.md does not exist at init\"\n        outputs:\n          - resource_map_present: \"Boolean true when {spec_folder}/resource-map.md exists, else false\"\n          - resource_map_known_context: \"When present: summarize the map by section with entry counts across READMEs, Documents, Commands, Agents, Skills, Specs, Scripts, Tests, Config, and Meta, plus a one-line theme summary for each section. When absent: 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n\n      step_resolve_canonical_names:\n        action: \"Resolve canonical research packet artifact names before classification\"\n        inspect_legacy:\n          - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/config.json\"\n          - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/state.jsonl\"\n          - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/strategy.md\"\n          - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/dashboard.md\"\n          - \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/.pause\"\n        migration_policy: \"dual-read / single-write for 4 weeks\"\n        on_legacy_read:\n          append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"migration\",\"legacyPath\":\"{legacy_path}\",\"canonicalPath\":\"{canonical_path}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n\n      step_acquire_lock:\n        action: \"Acquire the single-writer advisory lock before session classification\"\n        command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs acquire --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --packet-id {spec_folder}\"\n        on_acquire: \"Capture ownerPid from the JSON output and reuse it for every release below. If acquired=false, fail closed — another deep-research run already holds this packet.\"\n        note: \"Uses the promoted runtime/ loop-lock CLI (single source of truth: stale-lock reclaim, clean owner-scoped release). macOS/BSD locking is advisory — best-effort single-writer, not a hard mutex across host calls; stale-lock override is confirm-only or explicit recovery-only.\"\n        # Lock-cleanup contract: the lock file MUST be released on every terminal exit path that follows acquisition.\n        # Runtimes honoring step_acquire_lock are required to perform this cleanup before halting or pausing.\n        on_halt:\n          action: \"Release the lock before any terminal halt branch returns control\"\n          applies_to: [\"step_classify_session.on_invalid_state\", \"step_classify_session.on_completed_session\", \"step_preinit_spec_branch.conflict-detected\"]\n          command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid}; failures here are logged but do not block the halt\"\n        on_cancel:\n          action: \"Release the lock on user cancel or pause-sentinel detection before sentinel processing\"\n          command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid}; cancel completes regardless of cleanup result\"\n        on_workflow_exit:\n          action: \"Release the lock as the final step of any workflow exit path (success or failure)\"\n          command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/loop-lock.cjs release --lock-path {state_paths.lock_file} --owner-pid {captured_owner_pid}; idempotent — safe to invoke when already released\"\n\n      step_classify_session:\n        action: \"Classify the session before writing files\"\n        inspect:\n          - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n        classify:\n          fresh: \"None of the three state artifacts exist\"\n          resume: \"Config, JSONL, and strategy all exist and agree on topic/spec folder; missing wait-checkpoint fields are read as nextRunAt:null and remainingDelayMs:null\"\n          completed-session: \"Resume artifacts exist and config.status == 'complete'\"\n          invalid-state: \"Any partial, missing, or contradictory combination\"\n        outputs:\n          - session_state: \"fresh | resume | completed-session | invalid-state\"\n        on_resume:\n          # T-YML-DPR-01 / R50-001: Resume is a WRITE-PATH. Produces `iteration-NNN.md` + JSONL appends.\n          # Paired with T-DOC-03 Gate 3 trigger addition (resume, save context, save memory, /speckit:save).\n          gate3_classification: write-path\n          gate3_rationale: \"resume produces iteration-NNN.md writes and JSONL state-log appends\"\n          log: \"Auto-resume: state artifacts are complete and consistent. Continue the same lineage (sessionId unchanged, generation unchanged, no archive).\"\n          append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"resumed\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"parentSessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"lineageMode\":\"resume\",\"continuedFromRun\":{iteration_count},\"generation\":{generation},\"archivedPath\":null,\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n          skip_to: phase_loop\n        on_restart:\n          action: \"Archive the current research packet under the root-level research_archive/ tree and start a new lineage segment with a fresh sessionId and generation+1.\"\n          command: \"if [ -d {state_paths.packet_dir} ]; then mkdir -p {state_paths.archive_root} && mv {state_paths.packet_dir} {state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}; fi\"\n          set:\n            lineage_mode: \"restart\"\n            parent_session_id: \"{prior_session_id}\"\n            generation: \"{prior_generation + 1}\"\n          append_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"restarted\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"sessionId\":\"{session_id}\",\"parentSessionId\":\"{prior_session_id}\",\"lineageMode\":\"restart\",\"generation\":{generation},\"archivedPath\":\"{state_paths.archive_root}/{timestamp_slug}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n          skip_to: step_create_config\n        note_deferred_branches: \"fork and completed-continue are deferred and no longer runtime-supported in this release. The reducer still reads `lineageMode` from config for dashboards and analysis, but only `new`, `resume`, and `restart` are live. See deep-research/references/protocol/loop-protocol.md §Lifecycle Branch Contract for the one-session contract.\"\n        on_completed_session:\n          log: \"Prior session already completed. Do not route directly to synthesis; archive the completed research/ tree or start a fresh packet instead.\"\n          halt: true\n          message: \"Completed deep-research packet detected. Archive or replace the existing research/ tree before starting a new session.\"\n        on_invalid_state:\n          halt: true\n          message: \"Existing deep-research state is incomplete or contradictory. Repair or archive the invalid research packet before continuing.\"\n        on_fresh:\n          action: \"Proceed with a new session\"\n\n      step_resolve_session_id:\n        action: \"Resolve init session id from caller when supplied, else preserve the auto-generated fallback\"\n        branch_on: \"session_id\"\n        if_present:\n          bind:\n            session_id_init: \"{session_id}\"\n        if_absent:\n          bind:\n            session_id_init: \"{AUTO_SESSION_ID}\"\n\n      step_create_config:\n        action: \"Create deep-research-config.json from template\"\n        template: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-config.json\n        populate:\n          topic: \"{research_topic}\"\n          maxIterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n          minIterations: 3\n          # Semantic: newInfoRatio with negative-knowledge emphasis. See SKILL.md §\"Convergence Threshold Semantics\".\n          convergenceThreshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n          antiConvergence.convergenceMode: \"{convergence_mode}\"\n          antiConvergence.divergent: {}\n          stuckThreshold: 3\n          minIdeaObservations: 2\n          maxDurationMinutes: 120\n          specFolder: \"{spec_folder}\"\n          resource_map_present: \"{resource_map_present}\"\n          # Honor the parsed --no-resource-map flag from deep-research.md:73 (default true; false when flag is set).\n          # The markdown command parses $ARGUMENTS and binds {resource_map_emit} before this step runs.\n          resource_map.emit: \"{resource_map_emit}\"\n          createdAt: \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"\n          status: \"initialized\"\n          executionMode: \"auto\"\n          lineage.sessionId: \"{session_id_init}\"\n          lineage.parentSessionId: null\n          lineage.lineageMode: \"new\"\n          lineage.generation: 1\n          lineage.continuedFromRun: null\n          nextRunAt: null\n          remainingDelayMs: null\n        output: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n\n      step_create_state_log:\n        action: \"Initialize JSONL state log with config record\"\n        # Same parsed --no-resource-map flag honored here so config and state_log agree from line 1.\n        content: '{\"type\":\"config\",\"topic\":\"{research_topic}\",\"maxIterations\":{max_iterations},\"minIterations\":3,\"convergenceThreshold\":{convergence_threshold},\"antiConvergence\":{\"convergenceMode\":\"{convergence_mode}\",\"divergent\":{}},\"minIdeaObservations\":2,\"resource_map_present\":{resource_map_present},\"resource_map\":{\"emit\":{resource_map_emit}},\"createdAt\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"specFolder\":\"{spec_folder}\",\"nextRunAt\":null,\"remainingDelayMs\":null}'\n        output: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n\n      step_create_strategy:\n        action: \"Create strategy file from template with initial questions\"\n        template: .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/deep-research-strategy.md\n        populate:\n          topic: \"{research_topic}\"\n          key_questions: \"Derive 3-5 key questions from the research topic\"\n          known_context: \"None\"\n          known_context_summary: \"None\"\n          max_iterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n          convergence_threshold: \"{convergence_threshold}\"\n        output: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n\n      step_create_registry:\n        action: \"Initialize reducer-owned findings registry\"\n        content: '{\"openQuestions\":[],\"resolvedQuestions\":[],\"keyFindings\":[],\"ruledOutDirections\":[],\"metrics\":{\"iterationsCompleted\":0,\"openQuestions\":0,\"resolvedQuestions\":0,\"keyFindings\":0,\"convergenceScore\":0,\"coverageBySources\":{}}}'\n        output: \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n\n      step_enrich_strategy_context:\n        action: \"Ensure Known Context is written only after strategy.md exists\"\n        condition: \"prior_context_found\"\n        edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n        note: \"Append or replace the Known Context section with prior_context_summary and retained detail from prior_context\"\n\n      step_enrich_strategy_resource_map:\n        action: \"Inject resource-map status into Known Context after strategy.md exists\"\n        edit: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n        note: \"When resource_map_present is true, append the resource_map_known_context snapshot. When false, append 'resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate'.\"\n\n      step_detect_spec_present:\n        action: \"Classify late-INIT spec.md state after the durable research packet exists\"\n        inspect:\n          - \"{spec_folder}/spec.md\"\n          - \"{state_paths.lock_file}\"\n        classify:\n          no-spec: \"spec.md is absent before any pre-init mutation\"\n          spec-present: \"spec.md exists and approved host anchors are available for bounded mutation\"\n          spec-just-created-by-this-run: \"spec.md already carries this run's DR seed markers and should not be reseeded\"\n          conflict-detected: \"missing host anchor, duplicate markers, or generated-block ambiguity makes mutation unsafe\"\n        outputs:\n          - folder_state: \"no-spec | spec-present | spec-just-created-by-this-run | conflict-detected\"\n          - normalized_topic: \"Trim, lowercase, and collapse whitespace in research_topic before dedupe checks\"\n        append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"spec_check_result\",\"folder_state\":\"{folder_state}\",\"normalized_topic\":\"{normalized_topic}\",\"specPath\":\"{spec_folder}/spec.md\",\"lockPath\":\"{state_paths.lock_file}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n\n      step_preinit_spec_branch:\n        action: \"Run the bounded pre-init spec branch required by spec_check_protocol\"\n        protocol_reference: \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/references/protocol/spec-check-protocol.md\"\n        branches:\n          no-spec:\n            create: \"{spec_folder}/spec.md\"\n            seed_markers:\n              - \"<!-- DR-SEED:REQUIREMENTS -->\"\n              - \"<!-- DR-SEED:SCOPE -->\"\n            requirements_host: \"Seed Requirements from the research ask without broadening scope\"\n            scope_host: \"Seed Scope from the research ask without inventing implementation details\"\n            set:\n              folder_state: \"spec-just-created-by-this-run\"\n              validate_spec_doc: true\n            append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"spec_mutation\",\"event\":\"spec_seed_created\",\"folder_state\":\"spec-just-created-by-this-run\",\"anchors_touched\":[\"Requirements\",\"Scope\"],\"diff_summary\":\"Seeded Level 1 spec.md from research topic with DR seed markers.\",\"seed_markers\":[\"DR-SEED:REQUIREMENTS\",\"DR-SEED:SCOPE\"],\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n          spec-present:\n            edit: \"{spec_folder}/spec.md\"\n            set:\n              validate_spec_doc: true\n            idempotency_check:\n              host_anchor: \"Open Questions\"\n              normalized_match: \"Normalize the existing anchor text by lowercasing, stripping punctuation, collapsing whitespace, and trimming before comparing with {normalized_topic}.\"\n              if_match:\n                skip_append: true\n                append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"spec_mutation\",\"event\":\"spec_preinit_context_deduped\",\"folder_state\":\"spec-present\",\"anchors_touched\":[\"Open Questions\"],\"diff_summary\":\"Skipped duplicate pre-init topic append because normalized topic already exists in Open Questions.\",\"normalized_topic\":\"{normalized_topic}\",\"specPath\":\"{spec_folder}/spec.md\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n              if_no_match:\n                append_only:\n                  - host_anchor: \"Open Questions\"\n                    content: \"Add the normalized research topic only if it is not already present.\"\n                  - host_anchor: \"Research Context\"\n                    content: \"Add a bounded note that deep-research is active for this topic and that research/research.md remains canonical.\"\n                append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"spec_mutation\",\"event\":\"spec_preinit_context_added\",\"folder_state\":\"spec-present\",\"anchors_touched\":[\"Open Questions\",\"Research Context\"],\"diff_summary\":\"Appended bounded pre-init research context for the normalized topic.\",\"normalized_topic\":\"{normalized_topic}\",\"specPath\":\"{spec_folder}/spec.md\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n          spec-just-created-by-this-run:\n            verify_markers:\n              - \"<!-- DR-SEED:REQUIREMENTS -->\"\n              - \"<!-- DR-SEED:SCOPE -->\"\n            set:\n              validate_spec_doc: false\n            note: \"Treat already-seeded spec.md as a no-op guard and continue.\"\n          conflict-detected:\n            append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"spec_mutation\",\"event\":\"spec_mutation_conflict\",\"folder_state\":\"conflict-detected\",\"reason\":\"Pre-init spec.md mutation is ambiguous or unsafe.\",\"specPath\":\"{spec_folder}/spec.md\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\"}'\n            halt: true\n\n      step_validate_preinit_spec_doc:\n        action: \"Run targeted strict validation after any deep-research pre-init spec.md mutation\"\n        condition: \"validate_spec_doc\"\n        command: \"SPECKIT_RULES=FRONTMATTER_VALID,LEVEL_DECLARED,TEMPLATE_SOURCE,TEMPLATE_HEADERS,PLACEHOLDER_FILLED,ANCHORS_VALID,SPEC_DOC_INTEGRITY,TOC_POLICY bash .opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh {spec_folder} --strict\"\n        note: \"This enforces the authored-spec markdown structural contract without applying full-packet required-file or completeness checks to workflow-owned research artifacts. It uses the Node validation orchestrator, whose strict path was measured at about 108ms for a fresh Level 3 packet on the local harness.\"\n\n      step_telemetry_heartbeat_started:\n        action: \"Emit a single-loop started row in the orchestration status ledger\"\n        skip_when: \"config.fanout is present\"\n        canonical_lifecycle_event: \"iteration_start\"\n        command: |\n          node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n          import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n\n          import { appendJsonlIfChangedAtomic } from './.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/atomic-state.ts';\n          import observabilityEvents from './.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/observability-events.cjs';\n\n          const { appendObservabilityEvent } = observabilityEvents;\n          const config = JSON.parse(readFileSync('{state_paths.config}', 'utf8'));\n          const timestamp = '{ISO_8601_NOW}';\n          const sessionId = String(config.lineage?.sessionId ?? '{AUTO_SESSION_ID}');\n          const generation = Number(config.lineage?.generation ?? 1);\n          const observabilityPath = '{state_paths.packet_dir}/observability-events.jsonl';\n          const row = {\n            event: 'started',\n            label: 'single',\n            at: timestamp,\n            duration_ms: 0,\n            loop_type: 'research',\n            sessionId,\n            generation,\n            gauges: { iterations: 0, elapsed_ms: 0, score: 0 },\n          };\n\n          const appended = appendJsonlIfChangedAtomic('{state_paths.status_ledger}', row, {\n            diffData: { event: row.event, label: row.label, sessionId, generation, gauges: { iterations: 0, score: 0 } },\n            diffField: 'state_hash',\n          });\n          if (appended) {\n            try {\n              appendObservabilityEvent(observabilityPath, row, {\n                producer: 'deep-research-auto',\n                stream: 'single-loop-telemetry',\n                subject: { label: row.label, sessionId, generation },\n                event: row.event,\n                status: 'running',\n              });\n            } catch {}\n          }\n          EOF\n        working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n        outputs:\n          - status_ledger_started: \"A fan-out-shaped status row with label single and event started\"\n\n      step_init_complete:\n        log: \"Initialization complete. Config, state, and strategy files created.\"\n        set: { current_iteration: 1, current_segment: 1, stuck_count: 0 }\n\n  # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n  # PHASE 2: ITERATION LOOP\n  # ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n  phase_loop:\n    purpose: Dispatch agent iterations until convergence\n    repeat: true\n    max_repeats: \"{max_iterations}\"\n    steps:\n\n      step_read_state:\n        action: \"Read current state from JSONL and strategy\"\n        read:\n          - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n          - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n        extract:\n          - iteration_count: \"Count lines where type === 'iteration'\"\n          - current_iteration: \"iteration_count + 1\"\n          - current_segment: \"Latest segment_start event segment, else 1\"\n          - last_newInfoRatio: \"Extract newInfoRatio from last iteration record\"\n          - last_focus: \"Extract focus from latest iteration record, else 'none yet'\"\n          - ratio_prev: \"Extract newInfoRatio from second-latest iteration record, else 'N/A'\"\n          - ratio_latest: \"Extract newInfoRatio from latest iteration record, else 'N/A'\"\n          - next_focus: \"Extract 'Next Focus' section from strategy.md\"\n          - remaining_questions: \"Count unchecked items in 'Key Questions'\"\n          - remaining_questions_list: \"List unchecked key questions from strategy.md\"\n          - carried_forward_open_questions: \"Extract 'Carried-Forward Open Questions' section from strategy.md, else '[None yet]'\"\n          - answered_count: \"Count answered questions from strategy.md\"\n          - total_questions: \"Count total questions tracked in strategy.md\"\n          - resource_map_present: \"Extract boolean from deep-research-config.json, default false\"\n          - resource_map_prompt_line: \"If resource_map_present is true, return 'Resource map: prior-inventoried files are listed in {spec_folder}/resource-map.md; treat them as the exclusion set when hunting for net-new files; flag only missed-from-map candidates as gaps.' Else return 'Resource map: resource-map.md not present; skipping coverage gate.'\"\n          - lineage_context_prompt_line: \"If a refreshed lineage context summary exists from the previous iteration, return 'Lineage context refresh: {summary}'. Else use prior_context_summary from startup when available; otherwise return 'Lineage context refresh: none loaded yet.'\"\n          - least_explored: \"First unanswered question not covered by the most recent iteration focus, else first unanswered question\"\n          - last_3_summaries: \"Summarize the latest 3 iteration records as 'run N: focus (ratio)'\"\n          - latest_status: \"Extract status from latest iteration record, else 'none yet'\"\n          - nextRunAt: \"Extract nullable nextRunAt from deep-research-config.json, default null\"\n          - remainingDelayMs: \"Extract nullable remainingDelayMs from deep-research-config.json, default null\"\n          - min_iterations_present: \"Boolean true when deep-research-config.json has a numeric minIterations field\"\n          - min_iterations_missing_warning: \"Boolean true when minIterations is missing; use no floor and log a warning so older configs keep prior stop behavior\"\n          - min_iterations_raw: \"Extract numeric minIterations from deep-research-config.json when present, default 0\"\n          - effective_min_iterations: \"Clamp min_iterations_raw to the inclusive range 0..max_iterations; if min_iterations_raw exceeds max_iterations, use max_iterations\"\n          - min_iterations_clamped: \"Boolean true when min_iterations_raw > max_iterations\"\n          - min_iterations_guard_already_passed: \"Boolean true when state_log already contains event == 'min_iterations_guard_pass'\"\n          - convergence_mode: \"Extract antiConvergence.convergenceMode when it is one of 'default', 'off', 'sliding-window', or 'divergent'; default to 'default'\"\n          - convergence_mode_warning: \"Boolean true when antiConvergence.convergenceMode is present with an unsupported value; use 'default'\"\n          - rejected_patterns_count: \"Read registry.rejectedPatterns length when registry exists, else 0\"\n          - rejected_candidate_matches: \"Read registry.suppressedCandidates when registry exists, else []\"\n          - rejected_pattern_fuzzy_threshold: \"Read config.rejectedPatternFuzzyThreshold when present, else 0.85\"\n          - min_idea_observations: \"Read config.minIdeaObservations when present, default 2; clamp to 1..10\"\n          - observed_ideas_count: \"Read registry.observedIdeas length when registry exists, else 0\"\n          - promoted_ideas_count: \"Read registry.promotedIdeas length when registry exists, else 0\"\n          - promoted_ideas_list: \"Read registry.promotedIdeas idea text in rank order when registry exists, else []\"\n          - suppressed_ideas_count: \"Read registry.suppressedIdeas length when registry exists, else 0\"\n          - pivot_lineage: \"Summarize registry.divergence.completed and registry.divergence.overrides with pivot ids, source iterations, and selected focus; else 'none yet'\"\n          - saturated_directions: \"List registry.divergence.saturatedDirections; else 'none yet'\"\n\n      step_run_now_check:\n        action: \"Detect and consume a one-shot run-now sentinel before pause/convergence/dispatch\"\n        command: |\n          node <<'EOF'\n          const { appendFileSync, existsSync, renameSync, unlinkSync } = require('node:fs');\n\n          const stateLogPath = \"{state_paths.state_log}\";\n          const sentinelPath = \"{state_paths.run_now_sentinel}\";\n          const pausePath = \"{state_paths.pause_sentinel}\";\n          const timestamp = \"{ISO_8601_NOW}\";\n          const sessionId = \"{config.lineage.sessionId}\";\n          const generation = Number(\"{config.lineage.generation}\");\n          const run = Number(\"{current_iteration}\");\n\n          function append(event) {\n            appendFileSync(\n              stateLogPath,\n              `${JSON.stringify({\n                type: \"event\",\n                mode: \"research\",\n                run,\n                timestamp,\n                sessionId,\n                generation,\n                ...event,\n              })}\\n`,\n              \"utf8\",\n            );\n          }\n\n          if (existsSync(sentinelPath)) {\n            append({ event: \"run_now_requested\", sentinelPath });\n            if (existsSync(pausePath)) {\n              append({\n                event: \"run_now_rejected\",\n                reason: \"loop_paused\",\n                sentinelPath,\n                pauseSentinelPath: pausePath,\n              });\n            } else {\n              const claimPath = `${sentinelPath}.consuming.${process.pid}.${Date.now()}`;\n              try {\n                renameSync(sentinelPath, claimPath);\n                unlinkSync(claimPath);\n                append({\n                  event: \"run_now_accepted\",\n                  sentinelPath,\n                  dispatchEvent: \"iteration_start\",\n                });\n              } catch (error) {\n                if (!error || error.code !== \"ENOENT\") {\n                  throw error;\n                }\n              }\n            }\n          }\n          EOF\n        outputs:\n          - run_now_requested: \"Emitted when {state_paths.run_now_sentinel} exists at the loop boundary\"\n          - run_now_accepted: \"Emitted after the sentinel is atomically renamed and deleted before dispatch\"\n          - run_now_rejected: \"Emitted with reason loop_paused when pause takes precedence; sentinel remains present\"\n\n      step_check_pause_sentinel:\n        action: \"Check for pause sentinel file\"\n        check: \"Does {state_paths.pause_sentinel} exist?\"\n        if_exists:\n          log_event: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"userPaused\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"stopReason\":\"userPaused\",\"sentinelPath\":\"{state_paths.pause_sentinel}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n          message: \"Research paused. Delete research/.deep-research-pause to resume.\"\n          halt: true\n        if_not_exists:\n          proceed: true\n\n      step_validate_convergence_config:\n        action: \"Validate convergence floor settings when loading config\"\n        if_min_iterations_missing:\n          append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"config_warning\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"field\":\"minIterations\",\"fallback\":0,\"message\":\"minIterations missing; using no convergence floor for backward compatibility.\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n          log: \"minIterations missing; using no convergence floor for backward compatibility.\"\n        if_min_iterations_clamped:\n          append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"config_warning\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"field\":\"minIterations\",\"configured\":{min_iterations_raw},\"effective\":{effective_min_iterations},\"maxIterations\":{max_iterations},\"message\":\"minIterations exceeds maxIterations; clamping to the hard cap.\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n          log: \"minIterations exceeds maxIterations; clamping to the hard cap.\"\n        if_convergence_mode_invalid:\n          append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"config_warning\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"field\":\"convergenceMode\",\"fallback\":\"default\",\"message\":\"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n          log: \"Unsupported convergenceMode; using default convergence behavior.\"\n\n      step_graph_convergence:\n        action: \"Evaluate coverage-graph convergence before the inline 3-signal vote and persist the graph decision snapshot\"\n        bash: 'node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs --spec-folder \"{spec_folder}\" --loop-type \"research\" --session-id \"{config.lineage.sessionId}\" --convergence-mode \"{convergence_mode}\" --persist-snapshot --iteration \"{current_iteration}\"'\n        note: \"Run before the inline vote. STOP from the inline 3-signal vote is allowed only when the graph decision is STOP_ALLOWED or absent.\"\n        outputs:\n          - graph_decision: \"Tool decision value (CONTINUE | STOP_ALLOWED | STOP_BLOCKED), else null when unavailable\"\n          - graph_decision_json: \"JSON-encoded graph decision string, else null\"\n          - graph_signals_json: \"Tool signals object, else {}\"\n          - graph_blockers_json: \"Tool blockers array, else []\"\n          - graph_trace_json: \"Tool trace payload, else []\"\n          - graph_convergence_score: \"signals.blendedScore when present, else the best available graph score, else 0\"\n        append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"graph_convergence\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"decision\":{graph_decision_json},\"signals\":{graph_signals_json},\"blockers\":{graph_blockers_json},\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n\n      step_check_convergence:\n        action: \"Evaluate stop conditions and combine the inline 3-signal vote with graph convergence\"\n        algorithm: |\n          1. if iteration_count >= max_iterations: STOP (maxIterationsReached). This terminal cap bypasses quality-guard overrides; record failed guards/blockers as synthesis evidence instead of continuing.\n          2. if stuck_count >= config.stuckThreshold: STUCK_RECOVERY\n          3. if convergence_mode == \"off\": skip convergence stop candidates and continue unless a terminal cap, pause sentinel, or recovery halt has already fired.\n          4. if remaining_questions == 0: STOP (all_questions_answered)\n          5. GRAPH-ASSISTED COMPOSITE CONVERGENCE:\n               step_graph_convergence already recorded graph_decision, graph_signals_json, graph_blockers_json, and graph_convergence_score for this run.\n               The existing inline 3-signal vote still computes the inline STOP candidate and is not replaced.\n               signals = []\n               Filter: exclude iterations where status == thought from signal inputs (use only evidence iterations)\n               a) Rolling average (w=0.30, needs 3+ iterations):\n                  avg = mean(last 3 newInfoRatios)\n                  stop if avg < convergence_threshold\n               b) MAD noise floor (w=0.35, needs 4+ iterations):\n                  noiseFloor = MAD(all ratios) * 1.4826\n                  stop if latest ratio <= noiseFloor\n               c) Question entropy (w=0.35):\n                  coverage = answered / total questions\n                  stop if coverage >= 0.85\n               Redistribute weights for unavailable signals.\n               if weighted_stop_score > 0.60: inline_stop_candidate = true\n               Combined stop rule: STOP only if the inline 3-signal vote says STOP AND graph_decision is STOP_ALLOWED or absent.\n               if inline_stop_candidate and graph_decision == \"STOP_BLOCKED\":\n                 decision = \"BLOCKED\"\n                 reason = \"blockedStop\"\n                 stop_blocked = true\n                 blocked_by_json = JSON array derived from graph_blockers_json\n                 blocked_by_csv = comma-separated blocker names derived from graph_blockers_json\n                 gate_convergence_pass = false\n                 gate_convergence_score = graph_convergence_score\n                 gate_key_question_coverage_pass = no blocker named questionCoverage\n                 gate_evidence_density_pass = no blocker named sourceDiversity or evidenceDepth\n                 gate_evidence_density_sources = graph_signals_json.sourceDiversity or 0\n                 gate_hotspot_saturation_pass = true\n                 recovery_strategy = first blocker reason/message, else \"Collect deeper graph evidence before stopping.\"\n               else if inline_stop_candidate and (graph_decision == \"STOP_ALLOWED\" or graph_decision is absent):\n                 decision = \"STOP\"\n                 reason = \"composite_converged\"\n                 stop_blocked = false\n          6. else: CONTINUE\n          7. if decision == \"STOP\" and reason != \"maxIterationsReached\" and effective_min_iterations > 1 and iteration_count < effective_min_iterations:\n               decision = \"CONTINUE\"\n               reason = \"minIterationsNotReached\"\n               min_iterations_guard_blocked = true\n               min_iterations_guard_pass = false","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":723,"totalLines":724,"truncated":true}},"title":".opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml","time":{"start":1789366420517,"end":1789366420521}},"id":"prt_09e8cc1cc0017tm86ciHVsfGB4","sessionID":"ses_f6176138cffeODZD3dhSK78dPo","messageID":"msg_09e8ca452001644sJS5GpNu9E8"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789366422928,"sessionID":"ses_f6176138cffeODZD3dhSK78dPo","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-91b02261ba8d339c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"ls -la \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening/research/lineages/\" && ls -la \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening/research/lineages/glm\" 2>/dev/null; echo \"---alternatives---\"; ls \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening/research/alternatives/\""},"output":"total 0\ndrwxr-xr-x@  6 michelkerkmeester  staff  192 Sep 14 08:10 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 14 michelkerkmeester  staff  448 Sep 14 08:10 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 16 michelkerkmeester  staff  512 Sep 14 08:10 1789363775244-64o2qi-deepseek\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 23 michelkerkmeester  staff  736 Sep 14 08:10 1789363775244-64o2qi-luna\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 20 michelkerkmeester  staff  640 Sep 14 08:10 1789363775244-64o2qi-swe2\ndrwx------@  8 michelkerkmeester  staff  256 Sep 14 08:10 glm\ntotal 8\ndrwx------@ 8 michelkerkmeester  staff  256 Sep 14 08:10 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 6 michelkerkmeester  staff  192 Sep 14 08:10 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 2 michelkerkmeester  staff   64 Sep 14 08:10 .executor-state\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 michelkerkmeester  staff   96 Sep 14 08:10 containment\ndrwx------@ 7 michelkerkmeester  staff  224 Sep 14 08:10 deep-research-audit-ledger\ndrwx------@ 7 michelkerkmeester  staff  224 Sep 14 08:10 deep-research-effect-ledger\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  staff  423 Sep 14 08:10 invocation-metadata.json\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 michelkerkmeester  staff   96 Sep 14 08:10 locks-and-fencing-v1\n---alternatives---\nsynthesis.md\n","metadata":{"output":"total 0\ndrwxr-xr-x@  6 michelkerkmeester  staff  192 Sep 14 08:10 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 14 michelkerkmeester  staff  448 Sep 14 08:10 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 16 michelkerkmeester  staff  512 Sep 14 08:10 1789363775244-64o2qi-deepseek\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 23 michelkerkmeester  staff  736 Sep 14 08:10 1789363775244-64o2qi-luna\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 20 michelkerkmeester  staff  640 Sep 14 08:10 1789363775244-64o2qi-swe2\ndrwx------@  8 michelkerkmeester  staff  256 Sep 14 08:10 glm\ntotal 8\ndrwx------@ 8 michelkerkmeester  staff  256 Sep 14 08:10 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 6 michelkerkmeester  staff  192 Sep 14 08:10 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 2 michelkerkmeester  staff   64 Sep 14 08:10 .executor-state\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 michelkerkmeester  staff   96 Sep 14 08:10 containment\ndrwx------@ 7 michelkerkmeester  staff  224 Sep 14 08:10 deep-research-audit-ledger\ndrwx------@ 7 michelkerkmeester  staff  224 Sep 14 08:10 deep-research-effect-ledger\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 michelkerkmeester  staff  423 Sep 14 08:10 invocation-metadata.json\ndrwxr-xr-x@ 3 michelkerkmeester  staff   96 Sep 14 08:10 locks-and-fencing-v1\n---alternatives---\nsynthesis.md\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"ls -la \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening/research/lineages/\" && ls -la \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening/research/lineages/glm\" 2>/dev/null; echo \"---alternatives---\"; ls \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening/research/alternatives/\"","time":{"start":1789366422925,"end":1789366422928}},"id":"prt_09e8cc454001aGsu5cvm3fGo1F","sessionID":"ses_f6176138cffeODZD3dhSK78dPo","messageID":"msg_09e8ca452001644sJS5GpNu9E8"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1789366424345,"sessionID":"ses_f6176138cffeODZD3dhSK78dPo","part":{"id":"prt_09e8cd317001GGDvayNNxgK4J0","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"1cc0e6131ba475722e0249515f7e7108a8c00ee4","messageID":"msg_09e8ca452001644sJS5GpNu9E8","sessionID":"ses_f6176138cffeODZD3dhSK78dPo","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":39274,"input":12092,"output":247,"reasoning":55,"cache":{"write":0,"read":26880}},"cost":0.001811596}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1789366433552,"sessionID":"ses_f6176138cffeODZD3dhSK78dPo","part":{"id":"prt_09e8cf70d001R6Jk1EzVLTRAfg","messageID":"msg_09e8cd715001X5lZzJT2UR2IRu","sessionID":"ses_f6176138cffeODZD3dhSK78dPo","snapshot":"1cc0e6131ba475722e0249515f7e7108a8c00ee4","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789366437437,"sessionID":"ses_f6176138cffeODZD3dhSK78dPo","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-82750604ec2be839","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml","offset":724},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/.opencode/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n724:           8. if effective_min_iterations > 1 and iteration_count >= effective_min_iterations and min_iterations_guard_already_passed == false:\n725:                min_iterations_guard_pass = true\n726:           9. if decision == \"STOP\" and reason != \"maxIterationsReached\":\n727:                guardResult = checkQualityGuards(state, strategy)\n728:                if not guardResult.passed:\n729:                  log: \"Quality guard failed: {guardResult.violations}. Overriding STOP to CONTINUE.\"\n730:                  decision = \"CONTINUE\"\n731:           See convergence.md for full pseudocode and signal definitions.\n732:           Segment-aware convergence is experimental/reference-only; live workflow uses the current session as a single segment.\n733:         outputs:\n734:           - decision: \"STOP | BLOCKED | STUCK_RECOVERY | CONTINUE\"\n735:           - reason: \"Human-readable stop reason\"\n736:           - stop_blocked: \"Boolean marker set when graph convergence vetoes an inline STOP candidate\"\n737:           - blocked_by_json: \"JSON array of graph blocker names when decision == BLOCKED\"\n738:           - blocked_by_csv: \"Comma-separated graph blocker names when decision == BLOCKED\"\n739:           - gate_convergence_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail for the graph-assisted convergence gate\"\n740:           - gate_convergence_score: \"Numeric score recorded from graph convergence\"\n741:           - gate_key_question_coverage_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail derived from graph blocker coverage signals\"\n742:           - gate_evidence_density_pass: \"Boolean pass/fail derived from graph blocker evidence-depth signals\"\n743:           - gate_evidence_density_sources: \"Source-diversity count or equivalent evidence-depth proxy\"\n744:           - gate_hotspot_saturation_pass: \"Research placeholder gate; true unless an explicit blocker sets otherwise\"\n745:           - recovery_strategy: \"One-line hint describing the next research action when decision == BLOCKED or STUCK_RECOVERY\"\n746:           - min_iterations_guard_pass: \"Boolean true when the configured convergence floor has cleared for the first time\"\n747:           - min_iterations_guard_blocked: \"Boolean true when the configured convergence floor overrides a STOP candidate to CONTINUE\"\n748: \n749:       step_emit_min_iterations_guard_pass:\n750:         action: \"Persist a first-class event when the convergence floor clears\"\n751:         if_pass:\n752:           append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"min_iterations_guard_pass\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"iterationCount\":{iteration_count},\"minIterations\":{effective_min_iterations},\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n753:           log: \"Minimum iteration floor cleared for convergence stopping.\"\n754: \n755:       step_emit_blocked_stop:\n756:         action: \"Persist a first-class blocked_stop event when the legal-stop decision tree returns blocked\"\n757:         if_blocked:\n758:           append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"blocked_stop\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"blockedBy\":{blocked_by_json},\"gateResults\":{\"convergence\":{\"pass\":{gate_convergence_pass},\"score\":{gate_convergence_score}},\"keyQuestionCoverage\":{\"pass\":{gate_key_question_coverage_pass},\"answered\":{answered_count},\"total\":{total_questions}},\"evidenceDensity\":{\"pass\":{gate_evidence_density_pass},\"sources\":{gate_evidence_density_sources}},\"hotspotSaturation\":{\"pass\":{gate_hotspot_saturation_pass}}},\"recoveryStrategy\":\"{recovery_strategy}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n759:           log: \"Graph convergence blocked STOP. Failed blockers: {blocked_by_csv}. Recovery strategy: {recovery_strategy}\"\n760:           set:\n761:             decision: \"CONTINUE\"\n762:             reason: \"blockedStop\"\n763:             stop_blocked: false\n764: \n765:       step_handle_convergence:\n766:         action: \"Act on convergence decision\"\n767:         if_stop:\n768:           branch_on: \"convergence_mode == 'divergent' AND reason is in ['composite_converged', 'all_questions_answered']\"\n769:           if_divergent_eligible:\n770:             eligibility_contract:\n771:               required_decision: \"STOP\"\n772:               eligible_reasons: [composite_converged, all_questions_answered]\n773:               excluded_reasons: [maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, minIterationsNotReached, error, manualStop, userPaused]\n774:               fail_closed: \"Any missing or ambiguous reason uses if_existing_terminal_path without preparing a pivot.\"\n775:             steps:\n776:               step_prepare_divergent_pivot:\n777:                 action: \"Generate state-grounded research candidates and prepare or resume the pivot transaction\"\n778:                 command: |\n779:                   node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n780:                   import {\n781:                     buildResearchPivotPreparationInput,\n782:                     renderResearchPivotSeatPrompt,\n783:                   } from './.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/divergent-research-pivot.ts';\n784:                   import {\n785:                     preparePivotTransaction,\n786:                   } from './.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts';\n787: \n788:                   const input = buildResearchPivotPreparationInput({\n789:                     artifactRoot: '{state_paths.packet_dir}',\n790:                     configPath: '{state_paths.config}',\n791:                     stateLogPath: '{state_paths.state_log}',\n792:                     strategyPath: '{state_paths.strategy}',\n793:                     registryPath: '{state_paths.registry}',\n794:                     currentIteration: Number('{current_iteration}'),\n795:                     maxIterations: Number('{max_iterations}'),\n796:                     triggerReason: '{reason}',\n797:                   });\n798:                   const prepared = await preparePivotTransaction(input);\n799:                   const seatPrompts = prepared.status === 'pending'\n800:                     ? Object.fromEntries(prepared.missingSeats.map((seat) => [\n801:                         seat.id,\n802:                         renderResearchPivotSeatPrompt(seat, prepared.dispatchContext),\n803:                       ]))\n804:                     : {};\n805:                   process.stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify({\n806:                     ...prepared,\n807:                     seatPrompts,\n808:                     boundaryRejections: input.boundaryRejections,\n809:                   })}\\n`);\n810:                   EOF\n811:                 working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n812:                 outputs:\n813:                   - pivot_prepare_json: \"The complete parsed JSON result\"\n814:                   - pivot_prepare_status: \"status from the prepare result\"\n815:                   - pivot_id: \"pivotId from the prepare result\"\n816:                   - pivot_paths_json: \"paths from the prepare result as JSON\"\n817:                   - pivot_resumed: \"resumed from the prepare result\"\n818:                   - pivot_missing_seat_ids: \"missingSeats ids from a pending result\"\n819:                   - pivot_seat_001_json: \"The seat-001 mandate object from missingSeats\"\n820:                   - pivot_seat_002_json: \"The seat-002 mandate object from missingSeats\"\n821:                   - pivot_seat_003_json: \"The seat-003 mandate object from missingSeats\"\n822:                   - pivot_seat_001_prompt: \"seatPrompts['seat-001']\"\n823:                   - pivot_seat_002_prompt: \"seatPrompts['seat-002']\"\n824:                   - pivot_seat_003_prompt: \"seatPrompts['seat-003']\"\n825:                   - pivot_dispatch_context_json: \"dispatchContext from a pending result as JSON\"\n826:                 short_circuit: \"When status is completed or failed, skip all dispatch and record steps and bind this result as pivot_result.\"\n827: \n828:               step_dispatch_pivot_seat_001:\n829:                 action: \"Natively dispatch the analytical research direction-selection seat\"\n830:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending' or pivot_missing_seat_ids does not contain 'seat-001'\"\n831:                 capture_timing: true\n832:                 if_native:\n833:                   dispatch:\n834:                     agent: deep-research\n835:                     model: opus\n836:                     context_source: \"pivot_seat_001_prompt\"\n837:                   wait_for_completion: true\n838:                 failure_contract: \"A native dispatch failure binds status=rejected, a {name,message} error, and the measured timestamps/duration, then proceeds to step_record_pivot_seat_001.\"\n839:                 outputs:\n840:                   - pivot_seat_001_dispatch_status: \"fulfilled or rejected\"\n841:                   - pivot_seat_001_output_json: \"Raw native return serialized as JSON when fulfilled\"\n842:                   - pivot_seat_001_error_json: \"{name,message} when rejected\"\n843:                   - pivot_seat_001_started_at_iso: \"Dispatch start timestamp\"\n844:                   - pivot_seat_001_completed_at_iso: \"Dispatch completion timestamp\"\n845:                   - pivot_seat_001_duration_ms: \"Dispatch duration in milliseconds\"\n846: \n847:               step_record_pivot_seat_001:\n848:                 action: \"Durably record the seat-001 native dispatch outcome\"\n849:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending' or pivot_missing_seat_ids does not contain 'seat-001'\"\n850:                 command: |\n851:                   node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n852:                   import { recordPivotSeatResult } from './.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts';\n853:                   const status = '{pivot_seat_001_dispatch_status}';\n854:                   const outcome = status === 'fulfilled'\n855:                     ? { status, output: {pivot_seat_001_output_json}, startedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_001_started_at_iso}', completedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_001_completed_at_iso}', durationMs: Number('{pivot_seat_001_duration_ms}') }\n856:                     : { status: 'rejected', error: {pivot_seat_001_error_json}, startedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_001_started_at_iso}', completedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_001_completed_at_iso}', durationMs: Number('{pivot_seat_001_duration_ms}') };\n857:                   process.stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify(recordPivotSeatResult({ paths: {pivot_paths_json}, pivotId: '{pivot_id}', seat: {pivot_seat_001_json}, outcome }))}\\n`);\n858:                   EOF\n859:                 working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n860: \n861:               step_dispatch_pivot_seat_002:\n862:                 action: \"Natively dispatch the critical research direction-selection seat\"\n863:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending' or pivot_missing_seat_ids does not contain 'seat-002'\"\n864:                 capture_timing: true\n865:                 if_native:\n866:                   dispatch:\n867:                     agent: deep-research\n868:                     model: opus\n869:                     context_source: \"pivot_seat_002_prompt\"\n870:                   wait_for_completion: true\n871:                 failure_contract: \"A native dispatch failure binds status=rejected, a {name,message} error, and the measured timestamps/duration, then proceeds to step_record_pivot_seat_002.\"\n872:                 outputs:\n873:                   - pivot_seat_002_dispatch_status: \"fulfilled or rejected\"\n874:                   - pivot_seat_002_output_json: \"Raw native return serialized as JSON when fulfilled\"\n875:                   - pivot_seat_002_error_json: \"{name,message} when rejected\"\n876:                   - pivot_seat_002_started_at_iso: \"Dispatch start timestamp\"\n877:                   - pivot_seat_002_completed_at_iso: \"Dispatch completion timestamp\"\n878:                   - pivot_seat_002_duration_ms: \"Dispatch duration in milliseconds\"\n879: \n880:               step_record_pivot_seat_002:\n881:                 action: \"Durably record the seat-002 native dispatch outcome\"\n882:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending' or pivot_missing_seat_ids does not contain 'seat-002'\"\n883:                 command: |\n884:                   node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n885:                   import { recordPivotSeatResult } from './.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts';\n886:                   const status = '{pivot_seat_002_dispatch_status}';\n887:                   const outcome = status === 'fulfilled'\n888:                     ? { status, output: {pivot_seat_002_output_json}, startedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_002_started_at_iso}', completedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_002_completed_at_iso}', durationMs: Number('{pivot_seat_002_duration_ms}') }\n889:                     : { status: 'rejected', error: {pivot_seat_002_error_json}, startedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_002_started_at_iso}', completedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_002_completed_at_iso}', durationMs: Number('{pivot_seat_002_duration_ms}') };\n890:                   process.stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify(recordPivotSeatResult({ paths: {pivot_paths_json}, pivotId: '{pivot_id}', seat: {pivot_seat_002_json}, outcome }))}\\n`);\n891:                   EOF\n892:                 working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n893: \n894:               step_dispatch_pivot_seat_003:\n895:                 action: \"Natively dispatch the pragmatic research direction-selection seat\"\n896:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending' or pivot_missing_seat_ids does not contain 'seat-003'\"\n897:                 capture_timing: true\n898:                 if_native:\n899:                   dispatch:\n900:                     agent: deep-research\n901:                     model: opus\n902:                     context_source: \"pivot_seat_003_prompt\"\n903:                   wait_for_completion: true\n904:                 failure_contract: \"A native dispatch failure binds status=rejected, a {name,message} error, and the measured timestamps/duration, then proceeds to step_record_pivot_seat_003.\"\n905:                 outputs:\n906:                   - pivot_seat_003_dispatch_status: \"fulfilled or rejected\"\n907:                   - pivot_seat_003_output_json: \"Raw native return serialized as JSON when fulfilled\"\n908:                   - pivot_seat_003_error_json: \"{name,message} when rejected\"\n909:                   - pivot_seat_003_started_at_iso: \"Dispatch start timestamp\"\n910:                   - pivot_seat_003_completed_at_iso: \"Dispatch completion timestamp\"\n911:                   - pivot_seat_003_duration_ms: \"Dispatch duration in milliseconds\"\n912: \n913:               step_record_pivot_seat_003:\n914:                 action: \"Durably record the seat-003 native dispatch outcome\"\n915:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending' or pivot_missing_seat_ids does not contain 'seat-003'\"\n916:                 command: |\n917:                   node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n918:                   import { recordPivotSeatResult } from './.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts';\n919:                   const status = '{pivot_seat_003_dispatch_status}';\n920:                   const outcome = status === 'fulfilled'\n921:                     ? { status, output: {pivot_seat_003_output_json}, startedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_003_started_at_iso}', completedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_003_completed_at_iso}', durationMs: Number('{pivot_seat_003_duration_ms}') }\n922:                     : { status: 'rejected', error: {pivot_seat_003_error_json}, startedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_003_started_at_iso}', completedAtIso: '{pivot_seat_003_completed_at_iso}', durationMs: Number('{pivot_seat_003_duration_ms}') };\n923:                   process.stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify(recordPivotSeatResult({ paths: {pivot_paths_json}, pivotId: '{pivot_id}', seat: {pivot_seat_003_json}, outcome }))}\\n`);\n924:                   EOF\n925:                 working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n926: \n927:               step_finalize_divergent_pivot:\n928:                 action: \"Finalize the prepared pivot after all missing native seats are durable\"\n929:                 skip_when: \"pivot_prepare_status != 'pending'\"\n930:                 command: |\n931:                   node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n932:                   import { finalizePivotTransaction } from './.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/divergent-pivot.ts';\n933:                   process.stdout.write(`${JSON.stringify(finalizePivotTransaction({ paths: {pivot_paths_json}, pivotId: '{pivot_id}', resumed: {pivot_resumed} }))}\\n`);\n934:                   EOF\n935:                 working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n936:                 outputs:\n937:                   - pivot_finalize_json: \"The complete parsed final result\"\n938: \n939:               step_resolve_divergent_pivot_result:\n940:                 action: \"Use prepare's terminal result on resume/short-circuit, otherwise use finalize's result\"\n941:                 branch_on: \"pivot_prepare_status\"\n942:                 if_pending: { bind: { pivot_result: \"{pivot_finalize_json}\" } }\n943:                 if_completed_or_failed: { bind: { pivot_result: \"{pivot_prepare_json}\" } }\n944: \n945:               step_apply_divergent_pivot_result:\n946:                 action: \"Adopt a successful focus or fail closed to the existing synthesis path\"\n947:                 branch_on: \"pivot_result.status\"\n948:                 if_completed:\n949:                   set:\n950:                     next_focus: \"{pivot_result.restoredFocus}\"\n951:                     pivot_lineage: \"Pivot {pivot_result.pivotId} selected {pivot_result.selectedCandidate.id} from source iteration {current_iteration}.\"\n952:                     saturated_directions: \"{pivot_result.completedEvent.saturatedDirections}\"\n953:                   command: \"node .opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs {spec_folder}\"\n954:                   log: \"Divergent pivot {pivot_result.pivotId} restored focus to {pivot_result.restoredFocus}; continuing iteration {current_iteration}.\"\n955:                   proceed_to: step_rejected_pattern_cache\n956:                 if_failed:\n957:                   log: \"Divergent pivot {pivot_result.pivotId} failed closed ({pivot_result.failureReason}); proceeding to synthesis.\"\n958:                   skip_to: phase_synthesis\n959:             on_error:\n960:               log: \"Divergent pivot integration error; failing closed to the existing synthesis path.\"\n961:               skip_to: phase_synthesis\n962:           if_existing_terminal_path:\n963:             log: \"Loop stopping. Reason: {reason}\"\n964:             skip_to: phase_synthesis\n965:         if_stuck_recovery:\n966:           append_to_jsonl: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"stuckRecovery\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"stopReason\":\"stuckRecovery\",\"fromIteration\":{current_iteration},\"outcome\":\"recovered\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n967:           log: \"Stuck detected ({stuck_count} consecutive no-progress). Entering recovery.\"\n968:           set: { next_focus: \"RECOVERY: Widen scope. Try fundamentally different approach. Least-explored question: {least_explored}\" }\n969:           reset: { stuck_count: 0 }\n970:         if_continue:\n971:           log: \"Iteration {current_iteration}: Continuing. Focus: {next_focus}\"\n972: \n973:       step_rejected_pattern_cache:\n974:         action: \"Apply reducer-derived rejected-pattern suppression before dispatch candidate selection\"\n975:         read:\n976:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n977:           - \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n978:           - \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n979:         candidate_sources:\n980:           next_focus:\n981:             category: \"next-focus\"\n982:             values:\n983:               - \"{next_focus}\"\n984:               - \"{remaining_questions_list}\"\n985:               - \"{carried_forward_open_questions}\"\n986:           recovery:\n987:             category: \"recovery\"\n988:             values:\n989:               - \"{recovery_strategy}\"\n990:               - \"{least_explored}\"\n991:           ideas:\n992:             category: \"ideas\"\n993:             values:\n994:               - \"{promoted_ideas_list}\"\n995:             optional_file: \"{state_paths.packet_dir}/research-ideas.md\"\n996:         algorithm: |\n997:           Use registry.rejectedPatternIndex and registry.promotedIdeas from the latest\n998:           reducer pass as the source of truth.\n999:           Compare normalized exact text first. Then compare fuzzy similarity with\n1000:           rejected_pattern_fuzzy_threshold, but only when candidate and rejected categories\n1001:           are compatible. Remove suppressed candidates from next_focus, recovery, and ideas\n1002:           selection before rendering the dispatch prompt. If all candidates are suppressed,\n1003:           halt for operator input instead of reusing a rejected idea.\n1004:         outputs:\n1005:           - accepted_next_focus: \"First unsuppressed next-focus candidate, or null\"\n1006:           - accepted_recovery_candidate: \"First unsuppressed recovery candidate, or null\"\n1007:           - accepted_idea_candidate: \"First unsuppressed ideas candidate, or null\"\n1008:           - rejected_candidate_matches: \"Suppressed candidate diagnostics from registry.suppressedCandidates plus any current-step matches\"\n1009:         if_next_focus_suppressed:\n1010:           set: { next_focus: \"{accepted_next_focus || accepted_recovery_candidate || accepted_idea_candidate}\" }\n1011:           log: \"Rejected-pattern cache suppressed the prior candidate; dispatching the next accepted candidate.\"\n1012:         if_all_candidates_suppressed:\n1013:           halt: true\n1014:           message: \"All next-focus, recovery, and ideas candidates match active rejected patterns. Remove/reset the rejected pattern or provide a new focus.\"\n1015: \n1016:       step_ideas_backlog_lifecycle:\n1017:         action: \"Track reducer-owned observed/promoted/rejected idea lifecycle before dispatch\"\n1018:         read:\n1019:           - \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1020:           - \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n1021:           - \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1022:         lifecycle:\n1023:           observed_event: \"idea_observed\"\n1024:           promoted_event: \"idea_promoted\"\n1025:           rejected_event: \"idea_rejected\"\n1026:           min_observations: \"{min_idea_observations}\"\n1027:           authority: \"Leaf agents emit observations only; reducer emits promotions and owns ranking.\"\n1028:         validate:\n1029:           - \"If new leaf-authored output includes idea_promoted, fail validation; only reducer output may append idea_promoted.\"\n1030:           - \"If promoted_ideas_count > 0 and next_focus is empty or all questions are resolved, prefer the first unsuppressed promoted idea.\"\n1031:           - \"If suppressed_ideas_count > 0, do not render those ideas into dispatch context.\"\n1032:         outputs:\n1033:           - observed_ideas_count: \"Reducer-derived observed ideas count\"\n1034:           - promoted_ideas_count: \"Reducer-derived promoted ideas count after minIdeaObservations\"\n1035:           - suppressed_ideas_count: \"Reducer-derived rejected/suppressed ideas count\"\n1036:           - accepted_idea_candidate: \"First unsuppressed promoted idea, or null\"\n1037: \n1038:       step_normalize_pause_events:\n1039:         action: \"Normalize pause and recovery lifecycle events to the frozen STOP_REASONS enum at emission time\"\n1040:         stop_reasons_enum: [converged, maxIterationsReached, blockedStop, stuckRecovery, error, manualStop, userPaused]\n1041:         rule_pause_sentinel:\n1042:           raw_event_forbidden: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"paused\"}'\n1043:           canonical_event: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"userPaused\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"stopReason\":\"userPaused\",\"sentinelPath\":\"{state_paths.pause_sentinel}\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n1044:         rule_stuck_recovery:\n1045:           raw_event_forbidden: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"stuck_recovery\"}'\n1046:           canonical_event: '{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"stuckRecovery\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"run\":{current_iteration},\"stopReason\":\"stuckRecovery\",\"fromIteration\":{current_iteration},\"outcome\":\"recovered\",\"timestamp\":\"{ISO_8601_NOW}\",\"sessionId\":\"{config.lineage.sessionId}\",\"generation\":{config.lineage.generation}}'\n1047: \n1048:       step_marker_scan:\n1049:         action: \"H-2 loop-prevention guard: scan previous iteration's rendered prompt for nested research marker\"\n1050:         algorithm: |\n1051:           if current_iteration > 1:\n1052:             PREV_PROMPT_PATH = \"{state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{previous_iteration}.md\"\n1053:             if file_exists(PREV_PROMPT_PATH):\n1054:               PREV_PROMPT_FIRST_LINE = head -1 of PREV_PROMPT_PATH\n1055:               if PREV_PROMPT_FIRST_LINE matches ^(DEEP-REVIEW|DEEP-RESEARCH|CODE-REVIEW)$:\n1056:                 log \"ERROR: nested research-of-review loop detected (marker found in previous iteration prompt). Aborting.\"\n1057:                 halt with exit code 2\n1058:         note: |\n1059:           False-positive prevention: only matches when the first line is exactly one of the\n1060:           three canonical markers. Markers appearing in comments or body text are ignored.\n1061:           True-positive triggers only when a previous iteration's rendered prompt literally\n1062:           starts with a deep-loop marker, indicating a nested research-of-review dispatch.\n1063: \n1064:       step_dispatch_iteration:\n1065:         action: \"Dispatch one iteration via the selected executor\"\n1066:         resolve_executor:\n1067:           source: \"config.executor\"\n1068:           loader: \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts#parseExecutorConfig\"\n1069:         pre_dispatch:\n1070:           generate_summary: |\n1071:             STATE SUMMARY (auto-generated):\n1072:             Segment: {current_segment} | Iteration: {current_iteration} of {max_iterations}\n1073:             Questions: {answered_count}/{total_questions} answered | Last focus: {last_focus}\n1074:             Last 2 ratios: {ratio_prev} -> {ratio_latest} | Stuck count: {stuck_count}\n1075:             {resource_map_prompt_line}\n1076:             {lineage_context_prompt_line}\n1077:             Next focus: {next_focus}\n1078:           render_prompt_pack:\n1079:             template_path: \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/assets/prompt-pack-iteration.md.tmpl\"\n1080:             renderer: \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/prompt-pack.ts#renderPromptPack\"\n1081:             output_path: \"{state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md\"\n1082:             variables:\n1083:               state_summary: \"{state_summary}\"\n1084:               research_topic: \"{research_topic}\"\n1085:               current_iteration: \"{current_iteration}\"\n1086:               max_iterations: \"{max_iterations}\"\n1087:               next_focus: \"{next_focus}\"\n1088:               remaining_questions_list: \"{remaining_questions_list}\"\n1089:               carried_forward_open_questions: \"{carried_forward_open_questions}\"\n1090:               last_3_summaries: \"{last_3_summaries}\"\n1091:               pivot_lineage: \"{pivot_lineage}\"\n1092:               saturated_directions: \"{saturated_directions}\"\n1093:               state_paths_config: \"{state_paths.config}\"\n1094:               state_paths_state_log: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1095:               state_paths_strategy: \"{state_paths.strategy}\"\n1096:               state_paths_registry: \"{state_paths.registry}\"\n1097:               state_paths_iteration_pattern: \"{state_paths.iteration_pattern}\"\n1098:               state_paths_delta_pattern: \"{state_paths.delta_pattern}\"\n1099:         pre_dispatch_audit:\n1100:           skip_when: \"config.executor.type == 'native'\"\n1101:           call: \".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts#writeFirstRecordExecutor\"\n1102:           args:\n1103:             stateLogPath: \"{state_paths.state_log}\"\n1104:             executor: \"{config.executor}\"\n1105:             iteration: \"{current_iteration}\"\n1106:         branch_on: \"config.executor.type\"\n1107:         if_native:\n1108:           dispatch:\n1109:             agent: deep-research\n1110:             model: opus\n1111:             context_source: \"rendered_prompt_pack\"\n1112:           wait_for_completion: true\n1113:         if_cli_claude_code:\n1114:           command: |\n1115:             node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n1116:             import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n1117:             import { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\n1118: \n1119:             import { runAuditedExecutorCommand } from './.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts';\n1120:             import { resolveClaudePermissionMode } from './.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts';\n1121: \n1122:             const executor = {\n1123:               kind: 'cli-claude-code',\n1124:               model: '{config.executor.model}',\n1125:               reasoningEffort: '{config.executor.reasoningEffort}' === 'null' ? null : '{config.executor.reasoningEffort}',\n1126:               serviceTier: '{config.executor.serviceTier}' === 'null' ? null : '{config.executor.serviceTier}',\n1127:               sandboxMode: '{config.executor.sandboxMode}' === 'null' ? null : '{config.executor.sandboxMode}',\n1128:               timeoutSeconds: Number('{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}'),\n1129:             };\n1130:             const args = [\n1131:               '-p',\n1132:               readFileSync('{state_paths.prompt_dir}/iteration-{current_iteration}.md', 'utf8'),\n1133:               '--model',\n1134:               executor.model,\n1135:               '--permission-mode',\n1136:               resolveClaudePermissionMode(executor.sandboxMode),\n1137:               '--output-format',\n1138:               'text',\n1139:             ];\n1140:             if (executor.reasoningEffort) {\n1141:               args.push('--effort', executor.reasoningEffort);\n1142:             }\n1143: \n1144:             const dispatchFacts = {\n1145:               command: 'deep/research',\n1146:               mode: 'research',\n1147:               specFolder: '{spec_folder}',\n1148:               artifactDir: '{state_paths.packet_dir}',\n1149:               iteration: Number('{current_iteration}'),\n1150:               executorKind: '{config.executor.type}',\n1151:               branchId: '{config.executor.type}',\n1152:               sessionId: '{config.lineage.sessionId}',\n1153:               generation: Number('{config.lineage.generation}'),\n1154:             };\n1155:             const dispatchId = 'research-i{current_iteration}-g{config.lineage.generation}';\n1156:             process.exit(\n1157:               runAuditedExecutorCommand({\n1158:                 command: 'claude',\n1159:                 args,\n1160:                 cwd: '{repo_root}',\n1161:                 timeoutSeconds: executor.timeoutSeconds,\n1162:                 stateLogPath: '{state_paths.state_log}',\n1163:                 executor,\n1164:                 iteration: Number('{current_iteration}'),\n1165:                 receiptDir: '{state_paths.packet_dir}/dispatch-receipts',\n1166:                 dispatchId,\n1167:               }),\n1168:             );\n1169:             EOF\n1170:           working_directory: \"{repo_root}\"\n1171:           timeout_seconds: \"{config.executor.timeoutSeconds}\"\n1172:           wait_for_completion: true\n1173:           notes:\n1174:             - \"sandboxMode maps to permission-mode: read-only -> plan, workspace-write -> acceptEdits, danger-full-access -> bypassPermissions\"\n1175:             - \"claude-code has no serviceTier flag\"\n1176:             - \"claude-code supports --effort for reasoning depth\"\n1177:         if_cli_cursor:\n1178:           command: |\n1179:             node --import \"$(node -p \"require.resolve('tsx', { paths: ['.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime'] })\")\" --input-type=module <<'EOF'\n1180:             import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n1181:             import { createRequire } from 'node:module';\n1182:             import { runAuditedExecutorCommand } from './.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-audit.ts';\n1183:             import { resolveSandboxMode, resolveClaudePermissionMode } from './.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/executor-config.ts';\n1184:             import {\n1185:               snapshotOutOfScopeDirtyPaths,\n1186:               enforceWriteContainment,\n1187:             } from './.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/write-containment.ts';\n1188: \n1189:             // cursor-agent/devin/pi have no single-executor branch of their own, so\n1190:             // without this they silently degrade to native. The command builder is the\n1191:             // same one the fan-out lineage path uses, so the enforced model allowlist,\n1192:             // headless write-mode flags, and binary preflight stay one source of truth.\n1193:             // It throws (fail closed) when the binary is absent or the model is off the\n1194:             // allowlist, so a requested CLI executor never becomes native.\n1195:             const require = createRequire(import.meta.url);\n1196:             const { buildLineageCommand } = require('./.opencode/skills/sy