{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789366560410,"sessionID":"ses_f6176138cffeODZD3dhSK78dPo","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a4829f4001d432cd","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"L=\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening/research/lineages/1789363775244-64o2qi-deepseek\"; echo \"=== CONFIG ===\"; cat \"$L/deep-research-config.json\"; echo; echo \"=== STATE LOG (all, with line numbers) ===\"; nl -ba \"$L/deep-research-state.jsonl\"; echo; echo \"=== DELTA iter-001 ===\"; cat \"$L/deltas/iter-001.jsonl\"; echo; echo \"=== DELTA iter-003 (first 3 lines) ===\"; head -3 \"$L/deltas/iter-003.jsonl\""},"output":"=== CONFIG ===\n{\n  \"sessionId\": \"fanout-deepseek-1789363775244-64o2qi\",\n  \"topic\": \"Cheaper per-lane isolation than full git worktrees: sparse or partial checkouts, shallow and reference clones, overlay or copy-on-write filesystems, single worktree with per-lane write redirection, per-lane sandboxed working directories with a shared object store, and one-checkout exact-attribution variants. For each: setup cost, disk cost, attribution exactness, what breaks (symlinked dependency roots, workspace self-links, compiled entry-point guards, the churn detector), and whether git worktree move or relocation survives.\",\n  \"specFolder\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening\",\n  \"mode\": \"research\",\n  \"loopType\": \"research\",\n  \"maxIterations\": 3,\n  \"convergenceMode\": \"off\",\n  \"convergenceThreshold\": 0.05,\n  \"stuckThreshold\": 3,\n  \"stopPolicy\": \"max-iterations\",\n  \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n  \"generation\": 1,\n  \"executor\": {\n    \"kind\": \"cli-devin\",\n    \"model\": \"deepseek-v4-flash-max\",\n    \"reasoningEffort\": null,\n    \"permissionMode\": \"acceptEdits\",\n    \"sandboxMode\": \"workspace-write\"\n  },\n  \"artifactDir\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789363775244-64o2qi-attempt-1-deepseek/specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening/research/lineages/deepseek\",\n  \"resourceMapPresent\": false,\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-14T06:05:00Z\",\n  \"fileProtection\": {\n    \"deep-research-config.json\": \"immutable\",\n    \"deep-research-state.jsonl\": \"append-only\",\n    \"deep-research-strategy.md\": \"mutable\",\n    \"findings-registry.json\": \"auto-generated\",\n    \"deep-research-dashboard.md\": \"auto-generated\",\n    \"iterations/iteration-NNN.md\": \"write-once\",\n    \"deltas/iter-NNN.jsonl\": \"write-once\",\n    \"research.md\": \"workflow-owned\"\n  }\n}\n\n=== STATE LOG (all, with line numbers) ===\n     1\t{\"type\":\"config\",\"topic\":\"Cheaper per-lane isolation than full git worktrees: sparse or partial checkouts, shallow and reference clones, overlay or copy-on-write filesystems, single worktree with per-lane write redirection, per-lane sandboxed working directories with a shared object store, and one-checkout exact-attribution variants\",\"maxIterations\":3,\"convergenceThreshold\":0.05,\"stuckThreshold\":3,\"convergenceMode\":\"off\",\"stopPolicy\":\"max-iterations\",\"specFolder\":\"specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-deepseek-1789363775244-64o2qi\",\"lineageMode\":\"new\",\"generation\":1,\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-14T06:05:00Z\"}\n     2\t{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":1,\"run\":1,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"git-native alternatives vs repo anatomy\",\"findingsCount\":7,\"newInfoRatio\":1.0,\"noveltyJustification\":\"First evidence pass; repo anatomy and mechanism-to-surface mapping are new\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"q1\",\"q2\",\"q4\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[],\"ruledOut\":[{\"approach\":\"shallow clone (--depth 1)\",\"reason\":\"truncates history not tree; full 1.4 GB materialization remains; new repo boundary breaks sweep machinery\",\"evidence\":\"fanout-run.cjs:515,2715-2741\"},{\"approach\":\"reference/shared clone\",\"reason\":\"object sharing is already free under one repo; documented corruption hazard when source is pruned\",\"evidence\":\"git clone documentation\"},{\"approach\":\"partial clone (blob:none/tree:0)\",\"reason\":\"promisor fetches couple lane liveness to source location; breaks churn detector on relocation\",\"evidence\":\"write-containment.ts:398-400\"}],\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-14T06:20:00Z\",\"durationMs\":1200000}\n     3\t{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":2,\"run\":2,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"non-git mechanisms vs the attribution invariant\",\"findingsCount\":6,\"newInfoRatio\":0.9,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Attribution invariant, detector hard-fail vs fail-open split, and wrong-tree recreation are new; redirection restates a scored 3/10 decision\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"q3\",\"q4\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"q3\"],\"ruledOut\":[{\"approach\":\"CoW/overlay filesystem lane\",\"reason\":\"lane is not a git working tree: detector hard-fails or fails open, sweep cannot reclaim, git index coherence breaks\",\"evidence\":\"write-containment.ts:744-752\"},{\"approach\":\"single worktree with per-lane write redirection\",\"reason\":\"already scored 3/10 in ADR-003; executor levers make redirection a project, and ADR-005 watch is report-only\",\"evidence\":\"decision-record.md:276,480-486\"},{\"approach\":\"per-lane sandboxed dir with shared object store\",\"reason\":\"without a git identity the store is unreachable and the detector is blind; with one it is a clone or a worktree\",\"evidence\":\"write-containment.ts:702-752\"},{\"approach\":\"per-lane GIT_INDEX_FILE + checkout-index --prefix\",\"reason\":\"runner status calls use the repo default index, so the detector watches the shared checkout while the lane writes its own tree\",\"evidence\":\"write-containment.ts:398-400\"}],\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-14T06:40:00Z\",\"durationMs\":1200000}\n     4\t{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":3,\"run\":3,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"frontier comparison, relocation matrix, adoption path, web verification\",\"findingsCount\":6,\"newInfoRatio\":0.85,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Cost table, relocation matrix and adoption path are new; git-behavior claims upgraded from hypothesis to cited fact\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"q1\",\"q2\",\"q4\",\"q5\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"q1\",\"q2\",\"q4\",\"q5\"],\"ruledOut\":[],\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-14T07:00:00Z\",\"durationMs\":1500000}\n     5\t{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"synthesis_complete\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-deepseek-1789363775244-64o2qi\",\"parentSessionId\":\"fanout-deepseek-1789363775244-64o2qi\",\"lineageMode\":\"new\",\"generation\":1,\"run\":3,\"stopReason\":\"maxIterationsReached\",\"totalIterations\":3,\"questionsAnsweredRatio\":1.0,\"averageNewInfoRatio\":0.9167,\"synthesisPath\":\"research.md\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-14T07:10:00Z\"}\n\n=== DELTA iter-001 ===\n{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":1,\"run\":1,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"git-native alternatives vs repo anatomy\",\"findingsCount\":7,\"newInfoRatio\":1.0,\"noveltyJustification\":\"First evidence pass; repo anatomy and mechanism-to-surface mapping are new\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"q1\",\"q2\",\"q4\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[],\"ruledOut\":[{\"approach\":\"shallow clone (--depth 1)\",\"reason\":\"truncates history not tree; full 1.4 GB materialization remains; new repo boundary breaks sweep machinery\",\"evidence\":\"file:.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:515,2715-2741\"},{\"approach\":\"reference/shared clone\",\"reason\":\"object sharing is already free under one repo; documented corruption hazard when source is pruned\",\"evidence\":\"git clone documentation\"},{\"approach\":\"partial clone (blob:none/tree:0)\",\"reason\":\"promisor fetches couple lane liveness to source location; breaks churn detector on relocation\",\"evidence\":\"file:.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/write-containment.ts:398-400\"}],\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-14T06:20:00Z\",\"durationMs\":1200000}\n\n=== DELTA iter-003 (first 3 lines) ===\n{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":3,\"run\":3,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"frontier comparison, relocation matrix, adoption path, web verification\",\"findingsCount\":6,\"newInfoRatio\":0.85,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Cost table, relocation matrix and adoption path are new; git-behavior claims upgraded from hypothesis to cited fact\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"q1\",\"q2\",\"q4\",\"q5\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"q1\",\"q2\",\"q4\",\"q5\"],\"ruledOut\":[],\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-14T07:00:00Z\",\"durationMs\":1500000}\n","metadata":{"output":"=== CONFIG ===\n{\n  \"sessionId\": \"fanout-deepseek-1789363775244-64o2qi\",\n  \"topic\": \"Cheaper per-lane isolation than full git worktrees: sparse or partial checkouts, shallow and reference clones, overlay or copy-on-write filesystems, single worktree with per-lane write redirection, per-lane sandboxed working directories with a shared object store, and one-checkout exact-attribution variants. For each: setup cost, disk cost, attribution exactness, what breaks (symlinked dependency roots, workspace self-links, compiled entry-point guards, the churn detector), and whether git worktree move or relocation survives.\",\n  \"specFolder\": \"specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening\",\n  \"mode\": \"research\",\n  \"loopType\": \"research\",\n  \"maxIterations\": 3,\n  \"convergenceMode\": \"off\",\n  \"convergenceThreshold\": 0.05,\n  \"stuckThreshold\": 3,\n  \"stopPolicy\": \"max-iterations\",\n  \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n  \"generation\": 1,\n  \"executor\": {\n    \"kind\": \"cli-devin\",\n    \"model\": \"deepseek-v4-flash-max\",\n    \"reasoningEffort\": null,\n    \"permissionMode\": \"acceptEdits\",\n    \"sandboxMode\": \"workspace-write\"\n  },\n  \"artifactDir\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789363775244-64o2qi-attempt-1-deepseek/specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening/research/lineages/deepseek\",\n  \"resourceMapPresent\": false,\n  \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-14T06:05:00Z\",\n  \"fileProtection\": {\n    \"deep-research-config.json\": \"immutable\",\n    \"deep-research-state.jsonl\": \"append-only\",\n    \"deep-research-strategy.md\": \"mutable\",\n    \"findings-registry.json\": \"auto-generated\",\n    \"deep-research-dashboard.md\": \"auto-generated\",\n    \"iterations/iteration-NNN.md\": \"write-once\",\n    \"deltas/iter-NNN.jsonl\": \"write-once\",\n    \"research.md\": \"workflow-owned\"\n  }\n}\n\n=== STATE LOG (all, with line numbers) ===\n     1\t{\"type\":\"config\",\"topic\":\"Cheaper per-lane isolation than full git worktrees: sparse or partial checkouts, shallow and reference clones, overlay or copy-on-write filesystems, single worktree with per-lane write redirection, per-lane sandboxed working directories with a shared object store, and one-checkout exact-attribution variants\",\"maxIterations\":3,\"convergenceThreshold\":0.05,\"stuckThreshold\":3,\"convergenceMode\":\"off\",\"stopPolicy\":\"max-iterations\",\"specFolder\":\"specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-deepseek-1789363775244-64o2qi\",\"lineageMode\":\"new\",\"generation\":1,\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-14T06:05:00Z\"}\n     2\t{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":1,\"run\":1,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"git-native alternatives vs repo anatomy\",\"findingsCount\":7,\"newInfoRatio\":1.0,\"noveltyJustification\":\"First evidence pass; repo anatomy and mechanism-to-surface mapping are new\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"q1\",\"q2\",\"q4\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[],\"ruledOut\":[{\"approach\":\"shallow clone (--depth 1)\",\"reason\":\"truncates history not tree; full 1.4 GB materialization remains; new repo boundary breaks sweep machinery\",\"evidence\":\"fanout-run.cjs:515,2715-2741\"},{\"approach\":\"reference/shared clone\",\"reason\":\"object sharing is already free under one repo; documented corruption hazard when source is pruned\",\"evidence\":\"git clone documentation\"},{\"approach\":\"partial clone (blob:none/tree:0)\",\"reason\":\"promisor fetches couple lane liveness to source location; breaks churn detector on relocation\",\"evidence\":\"write-containment.ts:398-400\"}],\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-14T06:20:00Z\",\"durationMs\":1200000}\n     3\t{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":2,\"run\":2,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"non-git mechanisms vs the attribution invariant\",\"findingsCount\":6,\"newInfoRatio\":0.9,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Attribution invariant, detector hard-fail vs fail-open split, and wrong-tree recreation are new; redirection restates a scored 3/10 decision\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"q3\",\"q4\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"q3\"],\"ruledOut\":[{\"approach\":\"CoW/overlay filesystem lane\",\"reason\":\"lane is not a git working tree: detector hard-fails or fails open, sweep cannot reclaim, git index coherence breaks\",\"evidence\":\"write-containment.ts:744-752\"},{\"approach\":\"single worktree with per-lane write redirection\",\"reason\":\"already scored 3/10 in ADR-003; executor levers make redirection a project, and ADR-005 watch is report-only\",\"evidence\":\"decision-record.md:276,480-486\"},{\"approach\":\"per-lane sandboxed dir with shared object store\",\"reason\":\"without a git identity the store is unreachable and the detector is blind; with one it is a clone or a worktree\",\"evidence\":\"write-containment.ts:702-752\"},{\"approach\":\"per-lane GIT_INDEX_FILE + checkout-index --prefix\",\"reason\":\"runner status calls use the repo default index, so the detector watches the shared checkout while the lane writes its own tree\",\"evidence\":\"write-containment.ts:398-400\"}],\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-14T06:40:00Z\",\"durationMs\":1200000}\n     4\t{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":3,\"run\":3,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"frontier comparison, relocation matrix, adoption path, web verification\",\"findingsCount\":6,\"newInfoRatio\":0.85,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Cost table, relocation matrix and adoption path are new; git-behavior claims upgraded from hypothesis to cited fact\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"q1\",\"q2\",\"q4\",\"q5\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"q1\",\"q2\",\"q4\",\"q5\"],\"ruledOut\":[],\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-14T07:00:00Z\",\"durationMs\":1500000}\n     5\t{\"type\":\"event\",\"event\":\"synthesis_complete\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-deepseek-1789363775244-64o2qi\",\"parentSessionId\":\"fanout-deepseek-1789363775244-64o2qi\",\"lineageMode\":\"new\",\"generation\":1,\"run\":3,\"stopReason\":\"maxIterationsReached\",\"totalIterations\":3,\"questionsAnsweredRatio\":1.0,\"averageNewInfoRatio\":0.9167,\"synthesisPath\":\"research.md\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-14T07:10:00Z\"}\n\n=== DELTA iter-001 ===\n{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":1,\"run\":1,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"git-native alternatives vs repo anatomy\",\"findingsCount\":7,\"newInfoRatio\":1.0,\"noveltyJustification\":\"First evidence pass; repo anatomy and mechanism-to-surface mapping are new\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"q1\",\"q2\",\"q4\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[],\"ruledOut\":[{\"approach\":\"shallow clone (--depth 1)\",\"reason\":\"truncates history not tree; full 1.4 GB materialization remains; new repo boundary breaks sweep machinery\",\"evidence\":\"file:.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs:515,2715-2741\"},{\"approach\":\"reference/shared clone\",\"reason\":\"object sharing is already free under one repo; documented corruption hazard when source is pruned\",\"evidence\":\"git clone documentation\"},{\"approach\":\"partial clone (blob:none/tree:0)\",\"reason\":\"promisor fetches couple lane liveness to source location; breaks churn detector on relocation\",\"evidence\":\"file:.opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/lib/deep-loop/write-containment.ts:398-400\"}],\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-14T06:20:00Z\",\"durationMs\":1200000}\n\n===