{"type":"text","timestamp":1789367520774,"sessionID":"ses_f6176138cffeODZD3dhSK78dPo","part":{"id":"prt_09e9d797b001Uv5GZqOw7oDcbj","messageID":"msg_09e9ca99d0014v1gs0jlEtgsmh","sessionID":"ses_f6176138cffeODZD3dhSK78dPo","type":"text","text":"Lifecycle code seals it: `git worktree add --detach ... HEAD` (full 82,572-file checkout, no cone), SEVEN (not six) absolute→MAIN symlink provisions — including the `shared/dist` the earlier synthesis called missing — seed = per-file `copyFileSync` (no reflink, no clonefile), teardown = non-forced `git worktree remove` that must first clear untracked content. One last grep: the caller's seed paths (does the 101M untracked `node_modules` get copied per lane?) and the teardown force question.","time":{"start":1789367515515,"end":1789367520772}}}
