neage's write surface and therefore deferred, not skipped silently — recorded here).\n \n ## Key Questions\n \n-- [ ] q1: What does the 22.2 s/lane actually consist of (checkout vs seed vs provisions vs sweep vs teardown), and which legs fall with a checkout cone?\n+- [x] q1: What does the 22.2 s/lane actually consist of? — answered structurally (legs L1–L7); the leg WEIGHTS are carried forward (no instrumentation exists — f-102).\n - [ ] q2: Does a tighter, closure-computed cone (skill subtree, not wholesale `.opencode/`) beat the prior 62%/85% cuts? What does the lane's true read set cost?\n - [ ] q3: Is there a materialization mechanism with no shared repo state (no `extensions.worktreeConfig`, no `core.sparseCheckout`) — e.g. full-index partial materialization — and what does it cost the detector/containment paths?\n - [ ] q4: Do the prior mechanism rulings (redirection, CoW, partial/shallow/reference) survive their own code evidence, and what did the clonefile variant miss (inodes, first-status tax, ignored trees, ctime/index)?\n - [ ] q5: What does relocation actually pin (fencing, watermarks, receipts, `.git` pointer), what remains unmeasured (teardown, status tax, 28-worktree interference), and what changes in the prior adoption order?\n","additions":1,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening/research/lineages/glm/deep-research-strategy.md","time":{"start":1789368092710,"end":1789368092712}},"id":"prt_09ea63f8a001p9U2pC7VTEsSzp","sessionID":"ses_f6176138cffeODZD3dhSK78dPo","messageID":"msg_09ea61a74001Uv9WEPMhAaFSdk"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789368104803,"sessionID":"ses_f6176138cffeODZD3dhSK78dPo","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-b9ec4789d1ef3bd9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening/research/lineages/glm/deep-research-strategy.md","oldString":"## What Worked\n\n- (none yet)\n\n## What Failed\n\n- (none yet)\n\n## Exhausted Approaches\n\n- (none yet)\n\n## Next Focus\n\nIteration 1: cost decomposition — re-measure today's tree/object/lineage numbers read-only, and decompose the 22.2 s via `worktree-lifecycle.ts` (create/seed/publish/remove, timing instrumentation if any).\n\n## Carried-Forward Open Questions\n\n[None yet]","newString":"## What Worked\n\n- Read-only re-measurement over citation: today's tree (82,572 tracked, 1.7 G, `.opencode` 353 M, pack 2.06 GiB unchanged, 29 worktrees, sparse/worktreeConfig UNSET) adjudicates every number the prior synthesis cites — three of its counts were already stale.\n- Reading the provisioning code before pricing mechanisms: the 22.2 s decomposes into 7 legs, of which the checkout cone touches exactly one.\n\n## What Failed\n\n- Gateway-only state recording: the legacy-V1 projection drops mode/focus/route-proof, so `verify-iteration.cjs` fails `route_proof_missing`. Resolved by the validator's own sanctioned path (verify-iteration.cjs:15-18,254-257): the gateway's canonical event stays in the ledger, and the SAME canonical record (real timestamps) is appended to the state log, which the validator's last-record-wins + ledger-backing gate accepts. Root cause is deeper than the prior synthesis's L1: the `deep-research.ledger.iteration-completed` event schema's data carries no mode/focus/target_agent at all, so NO projection of it can ever pass route-proof. Event record: `events/iteration-001.result.json`.\n\n## Exhausted Approaches\n\n- Re-deriving the 22.2 s leg weights from the runner's own telemetry (no timing instrumentation exists).\n- Attributing `.opencode/node_modules` to tracked checkout, the 7-path provisioning, or the seed (all three disproven).\n\n## Next Focus\n\nIteration 2: challenge the mechanism rulings — what the 62%/85% cuts actually govern (tracked-only; the 101 MB bootstrap leg is invisible to them), whether a no-shared-state materialization (full-index partial materialization via skip-worktree) escapes the repository-wide `extensions.worktreeConfig` flip entirely, what the clonefile variant misses (index/ctime, ignored trees, inodes, first-status), and whether the wholesale-`.opencode` cone is the right granularity at all (sk-design = 148 M of the 353 M; measured lane read-closure ≈ 26–28 M).\n\n## Carried-Forward Open Questions\n\n- q1 weights: L1..L7 magnitudes (checkout vs dependency bootstrap vs statuses vs seed vs teardown) — unmeasurable from existing telemetry (zero instrumentation); needs the packet's stub-executor protocol or instrumentation.\n- Where the 101 MB `.opencode/node_modules` bootstrap leg actually comes from (executor plugin loader vs launch wrapper) — provenance unresolved, 5,454 entries, created at worktree birth."},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening/research/lineages/glm/deep-research-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening/research/lineages/glm/deep-research-strategy.md\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening/research/lineages/glm/deep-research-strategy.md\n@@ -20,25 +20,28 @@\n - [ ] q5: What does relocation actually pin (fencing, watermarks, receipts, `.git` pointer), what remains unmeasured (teardown, status tax, 28-worktree interference), and what changes in the prior adoption order?\n \n ## What Worked\n \n-- (none yet)\n+- Read-only re-measurement over citation: today's tree (82,572 tracked, 1.7 G, `.opencode` 353 M, pack 2.06 GiB unchanged, 29 worktrees, sparse/worktreeConfig UNSET) adjudicates every number the prior synthesis cites — three of its counts were already stale.\n+- Reading the provisioning code before pricing mechanisms: the 22.2 s decomposes into 7 legs, of which the checkout cone touches exactly one.\n \n ## What Failed\n \n-- (none yet)\n+- Gateway-only state recording: the legacy-V1 projection drops mode/focus/route-proof, so `verify-iteration.cjs` fails `route_proof_missing`. Resolved by the validator's own sanctioned path (verify-iteration.cjs:15-18,254-257): the gateway's canonical event stays in the ledger, and the SAME canonical record (real timestamps) is appended to the state log, which the validator's last-record-wins + ledger-backing gate accepts. Root cause is deeper than the prior synthesis's L1: the `deep-research.ledger.iteration-completed` event schema's data carries no mode/focus/target_agent at all, so NO projection of it can ever pass route-proof. Event record: `events/iteration-001.result.json`.\n \n ## Exhausted Approaches\n \n-- (none yet)\n+- Re-deriving the 22.2 s leg weights from the runner's own telemetry (no timing instrumentation exists).\n+- Attributing `.opencode/node_modules` to tracked checkout, the 7-path provisioning, or the seed (all three disproven).\n \n ## Next Focus\n \n-Iteration 1: cost decomposition — re-measure today's tree/object/lineage numbers read-only, and decompose the 22.2 s via `worktree-lifecycle.ts` (create/seed/publish/remove, timing instrumentation if any).\n+Iteration 2: challenge the mechanism rulings — what the 62%/85% cuts actually govern (tracked-only; the 101 MB bootstrap leg is invisible to them), whether a no-shared-state materialization (full-index partial materialization via skip-worktree) escapes the repository-wide `extensions.worktreeConfig` flip entirely, what the clonefile variant misses (index/ctime, ignored trees, inodes, first-status), and whether the wholesale-`.opencode` cone is the right granularity at all (sk-design = 148 M of the 353 M; measured lane read-closure ≈ 26–28 M).\n \n ## Carried-Forward Open Questions\n \n-[None yet]\n+- q1 weights: L1..L7 magnitudes (checkout vs dependency bootstrap vs statuses vs seed vs teardown) — unmeasurable from existing telemetry (zero instrumentation); needs the packet's stub-executor protocol or instrumentation.\n+- Where the 101 MB `.opencode/node_modules` bootstrap leg actually comes from (executor plugin loader vs launch wrapper) — provenance unresolved, 5,454 entries, created at worktree birth.\n \n ---\n \n *Machine-owned sections (iteration metrics, convergence signals) are updated by the lineage reducer inline; the workflow reducer at the packet root is out of this lineage's write surface, so this file carries the machine-owned state for this lineage.*\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening/research/lineages/glm/deep-research-strategy.md","patch":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening/research/lineages/glm/deep-research-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-write-containment-hardening/research/lineages/glm/deep-research-strategy.md\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/fanout-1789366204116-kfp53e-attempt-1-glm/specs/system-deep-loop/045-fanout-