{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789368509862,"sessionID":"ses_f6176138cffeODZD3dhSK78dPo","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a410ce420be9e0bc","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"F=\".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs\" && echo \"=== worktree identity/sweep: name-keyed? ===\" && grep -n \"FANOUT_WORKTREE_PREFIX\\|reclaim\\|sweep\\|resumable\" \"$F\" | head -14 && echo \"=== attribution source ===\" && grep -n \"attribution\\|dispatch-receipts\\|receiptDir\" \"$F\" | head -10 && echo \"=== family granularity, their 546M comparator ===\" && du -sh specs/system-deep-loop 2>/dev/null && git ls-tree -r HEAD specs/system-deep-loop | wc -l && git --version && date -u +%FT%T.000Z"},"output":"=== worktree identity/sweep: name-keyed? ===\n514:// prefix is what lets a sweep tell the trees this runner made from any other directory.\n515:const FANOUT_WORKTREE_PREFIX = 'fanout';\n519:// Lease budget for a lane's worktree. A sweep may treat a lease as stale only once its\n2687:  const [lifecycle, paths, publish, reclaim, lease] = await Promise.all([\n2691:    import('../lib/deep-loop/worktree-reclaim.ts'),\n2700:    sweepStagingResidue: publish.sweepStagingResidue,\n2701:    reclaimWorktrees: reclaim.reclaimWorktrees,\n2799: * so a failed setup leaves behind no directory a sweep would have to guess about.\n2814:  // create uses. It leads the label because the reclaim sweep recognizes a lane a resume may still\n2821:    prefix: FANOUT_WORKTREE_PREFIX,\n2882: * is what tells a later sweep the tree is a deliberate keep rather than debris. Nothing here\n3132:  // shared by every lane, so this run's trees are recognizable to its own sweep and to a later\n3155:    // One sweep, before any lane is dispatched: it reclaims what a dead run left under this\n3157:    // has to be read first. A failed sweep reports and leaves every entry alone rather than\n=== attribution source ===\n3476:      // Resolved once and reused below for write-containment attribution: a claude-code\n3563:      // tripping containment. Exclude them from attribution; everything outside\n3569:      // repo-local CLI config dir) is excluded from attribution the same way sibling\n=== family granularity, their 546M comparator ===\n357M\tspecs/system-deep-loop\n   12255\ngit version 2.50.1 (Apple Git-155)\n2026-09-14T06:48:29.000Z\n","metadata":{"output":"=== worktree identity/sweep: name-keyed? ===\n514:// prefix is what lets a sweep tell the trees this runner made from any other directory.\n515:const FANOUT_WORKTREE_PREFIX = 'fanout';\n519:// Lease budget for a lane's worktree. A sweep may treat a lease as stale only once its\n2687:  const [lifecycle, paths, publish, reclaim, lease] = await Promise.all([\n2691:    import('../lib/deep-loop/worktree-reclaim.ts'),\n2700:    sweepStagingResidue: publish.sweepStagingResidue,\n2701:    reclaimWorktrees: reclaim.reclaimWorktrees,\n2799: * so a failed setup leaves behind no directory a sweep would have to guess about.\n2814:  // create uses. It leads the label because the reclaim sweep recognizes a lane a resume may still\n2821:    prefix: FANOUT_WORKTREE_PREFIX,\n2882: * is what tells a later sweep the tree is a deliberate keep rather than debris. Nothing here\n3132:  // shared by every lane, so this run's trees are recognizable to its own sweep and to a later\n3155:    // One sweep, before any lane is dispatched: it reclaims what a dead run left under this\n3157:    // has to be read first. A failed sweep reports and leaves every entry alone rather than\n=== attribution source ===\n3476:      // Resolved once and reused below for write-containment attribution: a claude-code\n3563:      // tripping containment. Exclude them from attribution; everything outside\n3569:      // repo-local CLI config dir) is excluded from attribution the same way sibling\n=== family granularity, their 546M comparator ===\n357M\tspecs/system-deep-loop\n   12255\ngit version 2.50.1 (Apple Git-155)\n2026-09-14T06:48:29.000Z\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"F=\".opencode/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/fanout-run.cjs\" && echo \"=== worktree identity/sweep: name-keyed? ===\" && grep -n \"FANOUT_WORKTREE_PREFIX\\|reclaim\\|sweep\\|resumable\" \"$F\" | head -14 && echo \"=== attribution source ===\" && grep -n \"attribution\\|dispatch-receipts\\|receiptDir\" \"$F\" | head -10 && echo \"=== family granularity, their 546M comparator ===\" && du -sh specs/system-deep-loop 2>/dev/null && git ls-tree -r HEAD specs/system-deep-loop | wc -l && git --version && date -u +%FT%T.000Z","time":{"start":1789368509858,"end":1789368509860}},"id":"prt_09eac9d67001qzZxN39I6PB1ZC","sessionID":"ses_f6176138cffeODZD3dhSK78dPo","messageID":"msg_09eac234c001JnShdXT0qMynOP"}}
